��{"description": "Based on the research, outline the code structure for the weather app", "name": "Based on the research, outline the code structure for the weather app", "expected_output": "Code outline with main components and their responsibilities", "summary": "Based on the research, outline the code structure for the...", "raw": "Perfect! I've received substantial portions of the code. Let me now compile the final comprehensive answer with all the remaining components to provide you with the complete code outline.\n\n## **COMPLETE WEATHER APP CODE OUTLINE**\n\nBased on the comprehensive research and detailed project plan, here is the **complete code structure for the weather app**:\n\n---\n\n# **WEATHER APP - COMPLETE CODE STRUCTURE & ARCHITECTURE**\n\n## **DIRECTORY STRUCTURE**\n\n```\nweather-app/\n├── backend/\n│   ├── src/\n│   │   ├── config/\n│   │   │   ├── database.js          # Database connection & pooling\n│   │   │   ├── cache.js             # Redis cache configuration\n│   │   │   └── environment.js       # Environment variables\n│   │   ├── middleware/\n│   │   │   ├── authenticate.js      # JWT authentication\n│   │   │   ├── errorHandler.js      # Global error handling\n│   │   │   ├── rateLimiter.js       # Rate limiting\n│   │   │   └── logging.js           # Request logging\n│   │   ├── models/\n│   │   │   ├── User.js              # User schema & methods\n│   │   │   ├── City.js              # City schema & methods\n│   │   │   ├── UserCity.js          # User-City relationship\n│   │   │   ├── WeatherCache.js      # Weather data cache\n│   │   │   └── APILog.js            # API call logging\n│   │   ├── services/\n│   │   │   ├── AuthService.js       # Authentication logic\n│   │   │   ├── WeatherService.js    # Weather data operations\n│   │   │   ├── UserService.js       # User management\n│   │   │   ├── CityService.js       # City operations\n│   │   │   ├── CacheService.js      # Cache management\n│   │   │   └── ExternalWeatherAPI.js # External API integration\n│   │   ├── controllers/\n│   │   │   ├── AuthController.js    # Auth endpoints\n│   │   │   ├── WeatherController.js # Weather endpoints\n│   │   │   ├── UserController.js    # User endpoints\n│   │   │   └── CityController.js    # City endpoints\n│   │   ├── routes/\n│   │   │   ├── authRoutes.js        # /api/auth routes\n│   │   │   ├── weatherRoutes.js     # /api/weather routes\n│   │   │   ├── userRoutes.js        # /api/users routes\n│   │   │   ├── cityRoutes.js        # /api/cities routes\n│   │   │   └── index.js             # Route aggregation\n│   │   ├── utils/\n│   │   │   ├── validators.js        # Input validation\n│   │   │   ├── errorFormatter.js    # Error formatting\n│   │   │   ├── tokenGenerator.js    # JWT token generation\n│   │   │   └── weatherDataMapper.js # Data transformation\n│   │   ├── app.js                   # Express app setup\n│   │   └── server.js                # Server startup\n│   ├── tests/\n│   │   ├── unit/\n│   │   ├── integration/\n│   │   └── fixtures/\n│   ├── .env.example\n│   ├── package.json\n│   └── README.md\n│\n├── frontend/\n│   ├── src/\n│   │   ├── components/\n│   │   │   ├── Auth/\n│   │   │   │   ├── LoginForm.jsx\n│   │   │   │   ├── RegisterForm.jsx\n│   │   │   │   └── ProtectedRoute.jsx\n│   │   │   ├── Dashboard/\n│   │   │   │   ├── Dashboard.jsx\n│   │   │   │   ├── WeatherCard.jsx\n│   │   │   │   ├── CityGrid.jsx\n│   │   │   │   └── AddCityModal.jsx\n│   │   │   ├── Weather/\n│   │   │   │   ├── WeatherDetail.jsx\n│   │   │   │   ├── ForecastView.jsx\n│   │   │   │   └── CurrentWeatherDisplay.jsx\n│   │   │   ├── Search/\n│   │   │   │   ├── CitySearch.jsx\n│   │   │   │   └── SearchResults.jsx\n│   │   │   ├── Settings/\n│   │   │   │   ├── SettingsPage.jsx\n│   │   │   │   ├── PreferencesForm.jsx\n│   │   │   │   └── ThemeToggle.jsx\n│   │   │   ├── Common/\n│   │   │   │   ├── Header.jsx\n│   │   │   │   ├── Sidebar.jsx\n│   │   │   │   ├── LoadingSpinner.jsx\n│   │   │   │   ├── ErrorBoundary.jsx\n│   │   │   │   └── Notification.jsx\n│   │   │   └── Layout/\n│   │   │       └── MainLayout.jsx\n│   │   ├── pages/\n│   │   │   ├── LoginPage.jsx\n│   │   │   ├── RegisterPage.jsx\n│   │   │   ├── DashboardPage.jsx\n│   │   │   ├── WeatherDetailPage.jsx\n│   │   │   ├── SettingsPage.jsx\n│   │   │   └── NotFoundPage.jsx\n│   │   ├── store/\n│   │   │   ├── index.js\n│   │   │   ├── slices/\n│   │   │   │   ├── authSlice.js\n│   │   │   │   ├── weatherSlice.js\n│   │   │   │   ├── userSlice.js\n│   │   │   │   ├── citySlice.js\n│   │   │   │   ├── uiSlice.js\n│   │   │   │   └── settingsSlice.js\n│   │   │   ├── selectors/\n│   │   │   │   ├── authSelectors.js\n│   │   │   │   ├── weatherSelectors.js\n│   │   │   │   ├── citySelectors.js\n│   │   │   │   └── settingsSelectors.js\n│   │   │   └── thunks/\n│   │   │       ├── authThunks.js\n│   │   │       ├── weatherThunks.js\n│   │   │       ├── userThunks.js\n│   │   │       └── cityThunks.js\n│   │   ├── services/\n│   │   │   ├── api/\n│   │   │   │   ├── axiosInstance.js\n│   │   │   │   ├── apiClient.js\n│   │   │   │   ├── endpoints.js\n│   │   │   │   └── interceptors.js\n│   │   │   ├── auth/\n│   │   │   │   └── AuthService.js\n│   │   │   ├── weather/\n│   │   │   │   └── WeatherService.js\n│   │   │   ├── user/\n│   │   │   │   └── UserService.js\n│   │   │   └── city/\n│   │   │       └── CityService.js\n│   │   ├── hooks/\n│   │   │   ├── useAuth.js\n│   │   │   ├── useWeather.js\n│   │   │   ├── useCity.js\n│   │   │   ├── useSettings.js\n│   │   │   ├── useFetch.js\n│   │   │   └── useLocalStorage.js\n│   │   ├── styles/\n│   │   │   ├── index.css\n│   │   │   ├── variables.css\n│   │   │   ├── theme.css\n│   │   │   └── responsive.css\n│   │   ├── utils/\n│   │   │   ├── formatters.js\n│   │   │   ├── validators.js\n│   │   │   ├── constants.js\n│   │   │   └── helpers.js\n│   │   ├── config/\n│   │   │   ├── apiConfig.js\n│   │   │   └── appConfig.js\n│   │   ├── App.jsx\n│   │   └── index.jsx\n│   ├── .env.example\n│   ├── package.json\n│   ├── vite.config.js\n│   └── README.md\n│\n├── docker-compose.yml\n├── .gitignore\n└── README.md\n```\n\n---\n\n## **BACKEND COMPONENTS - DETAILED RESPONSIBILITIES**\n\n### **1. CONFIGURATION LAYER**\n\n#### **database.js** - Database Connection Management\n**Responsibility:** Initialize PostgreSQL/MongoDB connection pool, manage connections, handle reconnection logic\n```\n- Connection pooling with configurable pool size\n- Automatic reconnection on failure\n- Health check monitoring\n- Query execution wrapper\n- Connection lifecycle management\n```\n\n#### **cache.js** - Redis Cache Configuration\n**Responsibility:** Initialize and manage Redis cache for weather data and session storage\n```\n- Redis client initialization\n- TTL configuration for different data types (current: 1hr, forecast: 6hrs)\n- Cache key generation and management\n- Cache invalidation strategies\n- Connection pooling and error recovery\n```\n\n#### **environment.js** - Environment Variables\n**Responsibility:** Load, validate, and provide environment configuration\n```\n- Database credentials and connection strings\n- API keys for external weather services\n- JWT secrets and token expiry settings\n- Rate limiting configuration\n- CORS and security settings\n```\n\n---\n\n### **2. MIDDLEWARE LAYER**\n\n#### **authenticate.js** - JWT Authentication\n**Responsibility:** Verify JWT tokens and attach user context to requests\n```\n- Extract token from Authorization header\n- Validate JWT signature and expiry\n- Attach decoded user data to request\n- Handle token expiration and refresh\n- Support optional authentication routes\n```\n\n#### **errorHandler.js** - Global Error Handling\n**Responsibility:** Catch and format all application errors consistently\n```\n- Catch unhandled errors from routes and services\n- Format error responses with proper HTTP status codes\n- Log errors with context (user ID, endpoint, timestamp)\n- Distinguish between operational and programming errors\n- Sanitize sensitive information from error messages\n```\n\n#### **rateLimiter.js** - Request Rate Limiting\n**Responsibility:** Prevent abuse by limiting requests per IP/user\n```\n- General API limiter: 100 requests/15 minutes\n- Auth limiter: 5 login attempts/15 minutes\n- Weather API limiter: 50 requests/minute per user\n- Search limiter: 30 requests/minute per user\n- Redis-backed persistent rate limiting\n```\n\n#### **logging.js** - Request Logging\n**Responsibility:** Log all HTTP requests and responses for monitoring\n```\n- Log HTTP method, path, status code, and response time\n- Track user ID and IP address\n- Sanitize sensitive data (passwords, tokens)\n- Generate correlation IDs for request tracing\n- Structured logging for analytics\n```\n\n---\n\n### **3. DATABASE MODELS**\n\n#### **User.js** - User Account Management\n**Responsibility:** Define user schema and authentication methods\n```\nFields:\n- email (unique), password (hashed), username\n- firstName, lastName, profileImage, bio\n- preferences (temperature unit, theme, notifications)\n- emailVerified, passwordReset tokens\n- loginAttempts, accountLock, lastLogin\n- role (user/admin), isActive status\n\nMethods:\n- comparePassword() - Verify password during login\n- isAccountLocked() - Check if account is locked\n- incLoginAttempts() - Track failed login attempts\n- resetLoginAttempts() - Reset after successful login\n- createPasswordResetToken() - Generate password reset token\n- createEmailVerificationToken() - Generate email verification token\n```\n\n#### **City.js** - City Information\n**Responsibility:** Store city data with geographic coordinates\n```\nFields:\n- name, country, countryCode, state\n- latitude, longitude (for weather API calls)\n- timezone, population, isCapital\n- alternateNames, searchCount (popularity tracking)\n- timestamps for data freshness\n\nIndexes:\n- Compound unique index on (name, country, latitude, longitude)\n- Spatial index on coordinates for nearby city searches\n- Search count index for popular cities ranking\n```\n\n#### **UserCity.js** - User's City Preferences\n**Responsibility:** Link users to their tracked cities with custom settings\n```\nFields:\n- user (reference to User), city (reference to City)\n- isDefault (primary city), nickname (custom name)\n- alerts (temperature, precipitation, wind thresholds)\n- order (display sequence)\n\nMethods:\n- setAsDefault() - Make this the user's primary city\n- updateAlerts() - Modify alert thresholds\n- findUserCities() - Get all cities for a user\n- findDefaultCity() - Get user's primary city\n```\n\n#### **WeatherCache.js** - Cached Weather Data\n**Responsibility:** Store weather API responses to minimize external calls\n```\nFields:\n- city (reference), cacheType (current/forecast/hourly)\n- data (JSON weather information), source (API provider)\n- expiresAt (TTL index for auto-deletion)\n- hitCount (cache effectiveness metrics)\n\nMethods:\n- isExpired() - Check if cache data is stale\n- incrementHitCount() - Track cache usage\n- refresh() - Update with new data and reset TTL\n- findOrCreateCache() - Get or create cache entry\n- clearExpired() - Remove outdated entries\n```\n\n#### **APILog.js** - API Call Tracking\n**Responsibility:** Log all API requests for monitoring and debugging\n```\nFields:\n- endpoint, method, statusCode, responseTime\n- user (who made the call), requestSize, responseSize\n- errorMessage (if failed), ipAddress, userAgent\n- externalAPICall details (if calling third-party API)\n- TTL index for auto-deletion after 30 days\n\nPurpose:\n- Performance monitoring\n- Usage analytics\n- Error tracking and debugging\n- Rate limiting enforcement\n- Audit trail for security\n```\n\n---\n\n### **4. SERVICES LAYER**\n\n#### **AuthService.js** - Authentication Logic\n**Responsibility:** Handle user registration, login, and token management\n```\nMethods:\n- register(userData) - Create new user account\n  - Validate email uniqueness\n  - Hash password with bcrypt\n  - Generate JWT tokens (access + refresh)\n  - Return user profile and tokens\n\n- login(email, password) - Authenticate user\n  - Find user by email\n  - Verify password\n  - Update lastLogin timestamp\n  - Generate new tokens\n  - Return user and tokens\n\n- refreshToken(refreshToken) - Extend session\n  - Verify refresh token validity\n  - Generate new access token\n  - Return new token pair\n\n- changePassword(userId, oldPassword, newPassword) - Update password\n  - Verify old password\n  - Hash new password\n  - Save to database\n\n- resetPassword(email) - Initiate password reset\n  - Find user by email\n  - Generate reset token with 1-hour expiry\n  - Send reset email (integration point)\n  - Return reset token for frontend\n\n- logout(userId) - End session\n  - Optional: Add token to blacklist\n  - Clear client-side auth data\n```\n\n#### **WeatherService.js** - Weather Data Operations\n**Responsibility:** Fetch, cache, and serve weather data\n```\nMethods:\n- getWeatherByCityId(cityId, options) - Get current weather\n  - Check Redis cache first\n  - If cache miss, call external API\n  - Transform data to standard format\n  - Cache for 1 hour\n  - Return formatted weather data\n\n- getWeatherByCoordinates(lat, lon, options) - Weather by location\n  - Call external API with coordinates\n  - Transform response\n  - Return weather data\n\n- getWeatherForecast(cityId, days) - Get forecast\n  - Fetch forecast from external API\n  - Cache for 6 hours\n  - Return day-by-day forecast\n\n- getMultipleCitiesWeather(cityIds) - Batch fetch\n  - Parallel fetch for multiple cities\n  - Return array of weather data\n  - Optimize with concurrent requests\n\n- getWeatherAlerts(cityId) - Get active weather alerts\n  - Query external API for alerts\n  - Filter by location\n  - Return alert information\n\n- clearCache(city", "pydantic": null, "json_dict": null, "agent": "Crew Manager", "output_format": "raw", "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are Crew Manager. You are a seasoned manager with a knack for getting the best out of your team.\nYou are also known for your ability to delegate work to the right people, and to ask the right questions to get the best out of your team.\nEven though you don't perform tasks by yourself, you have a lot of experience in the field, which allows you to properly evaluate the work of your team members.\nYour personal goal is: Manage the team to complete the task in the best way possible."}, {"role": "user", "content": "\nCurrent Task: Based on the research, outline the code structure for the weather app\n\nThis is the expected criteria for your final answer: Code outline with main components and their responsibilities\nyou MUST return the actual complete content as the final answer, not a summary.\n\nThis is the context you're working with:\nPerfect! I have the detailed plan from our Project Planner. Let me present the complete project plan for building a weather app that shows forecasts for multiple cities:\n\n---\n\n# **DETAILED PROJECT PLAN: MULTI-CITY WEATHER APPLICATION**\n\n## **PROJECT OVERVIEW**\nBuild a comprehensive weather application that enables users to view weather forecasts for multiple cities with a focus on functionality, user experience, and code maintainability.\n\n---\n\n## **PHASE 1: PROJECT SETUP & PLANNING (Week 1)**\n\n### **Step 1.1: Requirements Gathering & Analysis**\n**Assigned to:** Project Manager + Requirements Analyst\n\n**Deliverables:**\n- Functional Requirements Document (FRD)\n- Non-Functional Requirements (performance, security, scalability)\n- User Stories and Use Cases\n- Technical Specifications\n\n**Key Requirements to Define:**\n- Number of concurrent users expected\n- Cities supported (fixed list vs. searchable)\n- Forecast duration (3-day, 7-day, 14-day)\n- Update frequency for weather data\n- Supported platforms (web, iOS, Android)\n- Performance benchmarks (page load time < 2s)\n\n**Dependencies:** None (project initiation)\n\n---\n\n### **Step 1.2: Technology Stack Selection**\n**Assigned to:** Tech Lead + Senior Architect\n\n**Deliverables:**\n- Technology Stack Document\n- Architecture Diagram\n- Development Environment Setup Guide\n\n**Recommended Stack:**\n- **Frontend:** React.js or Vue.js (web), React Native or Flutter (mobile)\n- **Backend:** Node.js/Express, Python/Django, or Java/Spring Boot\n- **Database:** PostgreSQL or MongoDB\n- **Weather API:** OpenWeatherMap, WeatherAPI, or NOAA\n- **Hosting:** AWS, Google Cloud, or Azure\n- **Version Control:** Git (GitHub/GitLab)\n- **CI/CD:** Jenkins, GitHub Actions, or GitLab CI\n\n**Dependencies:** Completion of Step 1.1\n\n---\n\n### **Step 1.3: Project Schedule & Resource Planning**\n**Assigned to:** Project Manager\n\n**Deliverables:**\n- Gantt Chart\n- Resource Allocation Matrix\n- Risk Register\n- Communication Plan\n\n**Key Milestones:**\n- Phase 1 Complete: End of Week 1\n- Phase 2 Complete: End of Week 3\n- Phase 3 Complete: End of Week 6\n- Phase 4 Complete: End of Week 8\n- Launch Ready: End of Week 9\n\n**Dependencies:** Completion of Step 1.1 and 1.2\n\n---\n\n## **PHASE 2: BACKEND DEVELOPMENT (Weeks 2-4)**\n\n### **Step 2.1: Database Schema Design**\n**Assigned to:** Database Architect + Backend Lead\n\n**Deliverables:**\n- Database Schema Diagram\n- Entity Relationship Diagram (ERD)\n- Database Setup Scripts\n\n**Key Entities:**\n- Users (id, username, email, password_hash, preferences)\n- Cities (id, name, latitude, longitude, country_code)\n- User_Cities (user_id, city_id, is_favorite, added_date)\n- Weather_Cache (city_id, temperature, humidity, forecast, last_updated)\n- API_Logs (api_call_id, timestamp, response_time, status_code)\n\n**Dependencies:** Completion of Step 1.2\n\n---\n\n### **Step 2.2: API Design & Documentation**\n**Assigned to:** API Architect + Backend Lead\n\n**Deliverables:**\n- API Documentation (Swagger/OpenAPI)\n- RESTful Endpoint Specifications\n- Authentication Strategy Document\n\n**Key Endpoints to Define:**\n- GET /api/v1/weather/current/:city_id\n- GET /api/v1/weather/forecast/:city_id?days=7\n- GET /api/v1/cities (searchable)\n- POST /api/v1/users/favorites (add favorite city)\n- DELETE /api/v1/users/favorites/:city_id\n- GET /api/v1/users/profile\n- POST /api/v1/auth/login\n- POST /api/v1/auth/register\n\n**Authentication:** JWT tokens with refresh mechanism\n\n**Dependencies:** Completion of Step 2.1\n\n---\n\n### **Step 2.3: Backend Core Development**\n**Assigned to:** Backend Developer(s) - 2-3 developers\n\n**Deliverables:**\n- Authentication Module (login, registration, JWT)\n- City Management Module\n- Weather Data Integration Module\n- User Preferences Module\n- Error Handling & Logging Framework\n\n**Key Components:**\n- User authentication service\n- Weather API client (with caching and rate limiting)\n- Database connection pooling\n- Error handling middleware\n- Request validation and sanitization\n- Logging and monitoring setup\n\n**Dependencies:** Completion of Step 2.2\n\n---\n\n### **Step 2.4: Weather API Integration**\n**Assigned to:** Backend Developer (API Integration Specialist)\n\n**Deliverables:**\n- Weather API Integration Module\n- Caching Strategy Implementation\n- Rate Limiting Implementation\n- API Response Transformation Layer\n\n**Implementation Details:**\n- Integrate with primary weather API (OpenWeatherMap)\n- Implement fallback to secondary API if primary fails\n- Cache weather data (1-hour TTL for current, 6-hour TTL for forecast)\n- Handle API rate limits gracefully\n- Transform API responses to standardized format\n- Error handling for API failures\n\n**Dependencies:** Completion of Step 2.3\n\n---\n\n### **Step 2.5: Backend Testing**\n**Assigned to:** QA Engineer + Backend Developers\n\n**Deliverables:**\n- Unit Test Suite (>80% code coverage)\n- Integration Test Suite\n- API Test Collection (Postman/Insomnia)\n- Test Results Report\n\n**Testing Scope:**\n- Unit tests for all business logic\n- Integration tests for database operations\n- API endpoint tests (happy path and error cases)\n- Authentication and authorization tests\n- Performance tests for API response times\n\n**Dependencies:** Completion of Step 2.4\n\n---\n\n## **PHASE 3: FRONTEND DEVELOPMENT (Weeks 2-5)**\n\n### **Step 3.1: UI/UX Design**\n**Assigned to:** UX Designer + UI Designer\n\n**Deliverables:**\n- Wireframes for all screens\n- High-fidelity Mockups\n- Design System & Component Library\n- User Flow Diagrams\n- Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG 2.1 AA)\n\n**Key Screens to Design:**\n- Login/Registration Screen\n- Dashboard (list of cities with current weather)\n- Detailed Weather Screen (7-day forecast)\n- City Search & Add Screen\n- User Settings/Preferences Screen\n- Favorites Management Screen\n\n**Design Considerations:**\n- Responsive design (mobile-first approach)\n- Dark mode support\n- Accessibility for color-blind users\n- Touch-friendly UI for mobile\n\n**Dependencies:** Completion of Step 1.1\n\n---\n\n### **Step 3.2: Frontend Project Setup**\n**Assigned to:** Frontend Lead\n\n**Deliverables:**\n- Frontend Project Repository\n- Build Configuration\n- Development Environment Setup Guide\n- Component Structure Documentation\n\n**Setup Tasks:**\n- Initialize React/Vue project with build tools\n- Configure webpack/Vite\n- Set up ESLint and Prettier\n- Configure environment variables\n- Set up testing framework (Jest, Vitest)\n- Create folder structure for components, pages, services, utilities\n\n**Dependencies:** Completion of Step 3.1 and Step 1.2\n\n---\n\n### **Step 3.3: Frontend Component Development**\n**Assigned to:** Frontend Developers - 2-3 developers\n\n**Deliverables:**\n- Reusable Component Library\n- Page Components\n- State Management Implementation\n- API Integration Layer\n\n**Components to Build:**\n- Weather Card Component\n- Forecast Component\n- City Search Component\n- Navigation Component\n- Settings Component\n- Loading Spinner & Skeleton Loaders\n- Error Boundary Component\n\n**State Management:** Redux, Zustand, or Context API\n- Implement global state for user data, selected cities, theme\n- Handle async API calls with proper loading and error states\n\n**Dependencies:** Completion of Step 3.2\n\n---\n\n### **Step 3.4: API Integration & Data Fetching**\n**Assigned to:** Frontend Developer (API Integration Specialist)\n\n**Deliverables:**\n- API Service Layer\n- Error Handling Implementation\n- Loading State Management\n- Data Caching Strategy (client-side)\n\n**Implementation Details:**\n- Create API service with axios or fetch\n- Implement request interceptors for auth tokens\n- Handle 401 responses (redirect to login)\n- Implement retry logic for failed requests\n- Client-side caching to reduce API calls\n- Loading indicators and error messages\n\n**Dependencies:** Completion of Step 3.3 and Step 2.5\n\n---\n\n### **Step 3.5: Frontend Testing**\n**Assigned to:** QA Engineer + Frontend Developers\n\n**Deliverables:**\n- Unit Test Suite (>80% code coverage)\n- Component Test Suite\n- E2E Test Suite\n- Test Results Report\n\n**Testing Scope:**\n- Unit tests for utility functions and helpers\n- Component tests (React Testing Library)\n- E2E tests for critical user flows (Cypress or Playwright)\n- Visual regression testing\n- Accessibility testing (axe-core)\n\n**Dependencies:** Completion of Step 3.4\n\n---\n\n## **PHASE 4: INTEGRATION & TESTING (Weeks 6-7)**\n\n### **Step 4.1: End-to-End Integration Testing**\n**Assigned to:** QA Lead + QA Engineers\n\n**Deliverables:**\n- E2E Test Suite\n- Integration Test Results\n- Bug Report with Severity Levels\n- Test Coverage Report\n\n**Test Scenarios:**\n- User registration and login flow\n- Add/remove favorite cities\n- View current weather for multiple cities\n- View detailed forecast\n- Search and add new cities\n- Update user preferences\n- Logout functionality\n- Cross-browser testing (Chrome, Firefox, Safari, Edge)\n- Mobile responsiveness testing\n\n**Dependencies:** Completion of Step 2.5 and Step 3.5\n\n---\n\n### **Step 4.2: Performance Testing**\n**Assigned to:** Performance Engineer + QA Engineer\n\n**Deliverables:**\n- Performance Test Report\n- Load Testing Results\n- Optimization Recommendations\n- Performance Baseline Document\n\n**Performance Metrics:**\n- Page load time (target: <2 seconds)\n- API response time (target: <500ms)\n- Time to Interactive (TTI)\n- Cumulative Layout Shift (CLS)\n- First Contentful Paint (FCP)\n- Load testing with 100+ concurrent users\n\n**Tools:** Lighthouse, JMeter, LoadRunner, or k6\n\n**Dependencies:** Completion of Step 4.1\n\n---\n\n### **Step 4.3: Security Testing**\n**Assigned to:** Security Engineer + QA Engineer\n\n**Deliverables:**\n- Security Test Report\n- Vulnerability Assessment\n- Penetration Testing Results\n- Security Recommendations\n\n**Security Checks:**\n- SQL Injection vulnerability testing\n- XSS (Cross-Site Scripting) testing\n- CSRF (Cross-Site Request Forgery) protection\n- Authentication and authorization testing\n- Sensitive data exposure\n- SSL/TLS configuration\n- OWASP Top 10 compliance\n\n**Tools:** OWASP ZAP, Burp Suite, or similar\n\n**Dependencies:** Completion of Step 4.1\n\n---\n\n### **Step 4.4: Bug Fixes & Optimization**\n**Assigned to:** Backend & Frontend Developers + QA Engineers\n\n**Deliverables:**\n- Fixed Bugs (all critical and high priority)\n- Performance Optimization Report\n- Code Refactoring Document\n- Final Test Results\n\n**Activities:**\n- Prioritize and fix bugs from testing phases\n- Optimize database queries\n- Implement code splitting and lazy loading\n- Compress assets and optimize images\n- Implement CDN for static assets\n- Database indexing optimization\n\n**Dependencies:** Completion of Step 4.3\n\n---\n\n## **PHASE 5: DEPLOYMENT & LAUNCH (Weeks 8-9)**\n\n### **Step 5.1: Deployment Infrastructure Setup**\n**Assigned to:** DevOps Engineer + System Administrator\n\n**Deliverables:**\n- Infrastructure as Code (IaC) Configuration\n- CI/CD Pipeline Setup\n- Deployment Documentation\n- Monitoring & Alerting Configuration\n\n**Infrastructure Setup:**\n- Set up production servers (AWS EC2, Google Cloud, or Azure)\n- Configure load balancers\n- Set up SSL/TLS certificates\n- Configure firewall rules and security groups\n- Set up database backups and recovery procedures\n- Implement monitoring (Prometheus, DataDog, New Relic)\n- Set up log aggregation (ELK Stack, Splunk)\n\n**CI/CD Pipeline:**\n- Automated testing on every commit\n- Build automation\n- Automated deployment to staging\n- Manual approval for production deployment\n- Rollback procedures\n\n**Dependencies:** Completion of Step 4.4\n\n---\n\n### **Step 5.2: Pre-Launch Testing**\n**Assigned to:** QA Team + DevOps Engineer\n\n**Deliverables:**\n- Staging Environment Test Report\n- Production Readiness Checklist\n- Launch Sign-Off Document\n- Rollback Plan\n\n**Pre-Launch Activities:**\n- Deploy to staging environment\n- Run full regression test suite\n- Verify all monitoring and alerting\n- Test backup and recovery procedures\n- Verify SSL certificates\n- Check DNS configuration\n- Performance testing in production-like environment\n- Security scan in staging\n\n**Dependencies:** Completion of Step 5.1\n\n---\n\n### **Step 5.3: Production Deployment**\n**Assigned to:** DevOps Engineer + Tech Lead\n\n**Deliverables:**\n- Deployment Completion Report\n- Production Verification Report\n- Launch Announcement\n- Incident Response Plan\n\n**Deployment Process:**\n- Blue-green deployment or canary deployment strategy\n- Monitor error rates and performance metrics during deployment\n- Have rollback plan ready\n- Notify support team of launch\n- Monitor first 24 hours closely\n- Collect user feedback\n\n**Dependencies:** Completion of Step 5.2\n\n---\n\n### **Step 5.4: Post-Launch Monitoring & Support**\n**Assigned to:** DevOps Engineer + Support Team + Backend Developer\n\n**Deliverables:**\n- Launch Report\n- Monitoring Dashboard\n- Support Runbook\n- Post-Launch Issue Log\n\n**Post-Launch Activities:**\n- Monitor application performance\n- Track error rates and exceptions\n- Respond to user-reported issues\n- Optimize based on real-world usage patterns\n- Collect analytics on user behavior\n- Plan for iterative improvements\n\n**Dependencies:** Completion of Step 5.3\n\n---\n\n## **PHASE 6: DOCUMENTATION & KNOWLEDGE TRANSFER (Week 9)**\n\n### **Step 6.1: Technical Documentation**\n**Assigned to:** Tech Lead + Senior Developers\n\n**Deliverables:**\n- Architecture Documentation\n- API Documentation (Swagger/OpenAPI)\n- Database Documentation\n- Deployment Guide\n- Troubleshooting Guide\n\n**Documentation Includes:**\n- System architecture overview\n- Component diagrams\n- Sequence diagrams for key flows\n- Database schema documentation\n- API endpoint reference\n- Environment setup guide\n- Deployment procedures\n- Common issues and solutions\n\n**Dependencies:** Completion of Phase 5\n\n---\n\n### **Step 6.2: User Documentation**\n**Assigned to:** Technical Writer + Product Manager\n\n**Deliverables:**\n- User Guide\n- FAQ Document\n- Video Tutorials\n- In-App Help Content\n\n**Documentation Includes:**\n- How to register and login\n- How to add/remove favorite cities\n- How to interpret weather forecasts\n- How to customize preferences\n- Troubleshooting common issues\n- FAQ section\n\n**Dependencies:** Completion of Phase 5\n\n---\n\n### **Step 6.3: Knowledge Transfer & Team Training**\n**Assigned to:** Tech Lead + Project Manager\n\n**Deliverables:**\n- Training Materials\n- Training Sessions Completed\n- Knowledge Transfer Report\n\n**Training Topics:**\n- Architecture overview\n- Codebase walkthrough\n- Deployment procedures\n- Monitoring and alerting\n- Incident response procedures\n- Development workflow and best practices\n\n**Dependencies:** Completion of Step 6.1 and 6.2\n\n---\n\n## **TEAM STRUCTURE & ROLES**\n\n### **Core Team Members:**\n\n| Role | Responsibility |\n|------|-----------------|\n| **Project Manager** | Overall project coordination, stakeholder communication, risk management, timeline tracking |\n| **Tech Lead/Architect** | Technology decisions, architecture design, code quality oversight, technical mentoring |\n| **Backend Developers (2-3)** | API development, database implementation, weather API integration, backend testing |\n| **Frontend Developers (2-3)** | UI component development, state management, API integration, frontend testing |\n| **DevOps Engineer** | Infrastructure setup, CI/CD pipeline, deployment management, monitoring and logging |\n| **QA Lead & QA Engineers (2)** | Test planning, test case development, manual and automated testing, bug tracking |\n| **UI/UX Designer** | Wireframe design, high-fidelity mockups, design system creation, user experience optimization |\n| **Database Architect** | Database schema design, query optimization, backup and recovery planning |\n| **Security Engineer (Part-time)** | Security requirements, penetration testing, vulnerability assessment |\n| **Technical Writer** | Documentation creation, user guides, API documentation\n\n----------\n\nPerfect! I've successfully delegated the research task to our Research Specialist. They've provided comprehensive findings on weather app development. Let me ensure we have the complete content by presenting their detailed research findings:\n\n---\n\n# **COMPREHENSIVE WEATHER APPLICATION DEVELOPMENT GUIDE**\n\n## **1. WEATHER API COMPARISON AND ANALYSIS**\n\n### **1.1 OpenWeatherMap API**\n\n**Overview:**\nOpenWeatherMap is one of the most popular weather data providers with extensive coverage and multiple API endpoints.\n\n**Key Features:**\n- Current weather data\n- 5-day and 16-day forecasts\n- Historical data\n- Weather alerts\n- Air quality data\n- UV index\n- Geocoding services\n- Multiple language support\n- Real-time updates\n\n**Pricing Tiers:**\n- **Free Tier**: 1,000 calls/day, 60 calls/minute\n  - Current weather\n  - 5-day forecast (3-hour step)\n  - Limited historical data\n- **Professional Tier**: Starting at $40/month\n  - 100,000 calls/month\n  - 16-day forecast\n  - Access to all historical data\n  - Priority support\n- **Enterprise**: Custom pricing\n  - Unlimited calls\n  - Dedicated support\n  - SLA guarantee\n\n**API Response Example:**\n```json\n{\n  \"coord\": {\"lon\": -74.006, \"lat\": 40.7143},\n  \"weather\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": 500,\n      \"main\": \"Rain\",\n      \"description\": \"light rain\",\n      \"icon\": \"10d\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"main\": {\n    \"temp\": 282.55,\n    \"feels_like\": 281.86,\n    \"temp_min\": 280.37,\n    \"temp_max\": 284.26,\n    \"pressure\": 1023,\n    \"humidity\": 100\n  },\n  \"visibility\": 10000,\n  \"wind\": {\n    \"speed\": 4.1,\n    \"deg\": 80\n  },\n  \"clouds\": {\"all\": 90},\n  \"dt\": 1605824400,\n  \"sys\": {\n    \"type\": 2,\n    \"id\": 2019646,\n    \"country\": \"US\",\n    \"sunrise\": 1605791400,\n    \"sunset\": 1605824400\n  },\n  \"timezone\": -18000,\n  \"id\": 5128581,\n  \"name\": \"New York\",\n  \"cod\": 200\n}\n```\n\n**Pros:**\n- Extensive historical data\n- Comprehensive weather parameters\n- Well-documented API\n- Large developer community\n- Reliable uptime\n- Multiple data sources\n\n**Cons:**\n- Rate limits on free tier\n- API key management required\n- Premium features require paid subscription\n- Some features have additional costs\n\n---\n\n### **1.2 WeatherAPI**\n\n**Overview:**\nWeatherAPI provides a simpler, developer-friendly alternative with generous free tier.\n\n**Key Features:**\n- Current weather\n- 10-day forecast\n- Hourly forecast\n- Air quality data\n- Alerts\n- Astronomy data\n- Sports data\n- Timezone information\n- Alerts and notifications\n\n**Pricing Tiers:**\n- **Free Tier**: 1,000,000 calls/month\n  - Current weather\n  - 10-day forecast\n  - 24-hour hourly forecast\n  - Air quality data\n  - Astronomy data\n- **Pro Tier**: $9.99/month\n  - 20-day forecast\n  - 384-hour hourly forecast\n  - Historical data (30 years)\n- **Business Tier**: $99/month\n  - 30-day forecast\n  - Full historical data\n  - Bulk operations\n  - Priority support\n\n**API Response Example:**\n```json\n{\n  \"location\": {\n    \"name\": \"New York\",\n    \"region\": \"New York\",\n    \"country\": \"United States\",\n    \"lat\": 40.71,\n    \"lon\": -74.01,\n    \"tz_id\": \"America/New_York\",\n    \"localtime_epoch\": 1605824400,\n    \"localtime\": \"2020-11-20 10:00\"\n  },\n  \"current\": {\n    \"last_updated_epoch\": 1605824400,\n    \"last_updated\": \"2020-11-20 10:00\",\n    \"temp_c\": 9.4,\n    \"temp_f\": 48.9,\n    \"is_day\": 1,\n    \"condition\": {\n      \"text\": \"Partly cloudy\",\n      \"icon\": \"//cdn.weatherapi.com/weather/128x128/day/116.png\",\n      \"code\": 1003\n    },\n    \"wind_mph\": 9.2,\n    \"wind_kph\": 14.8,\n    \"wind_degree\": 80,\n    \"wind_dir\": \"E\",\n    \"pressure_mb\": 1023,\n    \"pressure_in\": 30.21,\n    \"precip_mm\": 0,\n    \"precip_in\": 0,\n    \"humidity\": 72,\n    \"cloud\": 50,\n    \"feelslike_c\": 6.5,\n    \"feelslike_f\": 43.7,\n    \"vis_km\": 10,\n    \"vis_miles\": 6.2,\n    \"uv\": 2.1,\n    \"gust_mph\": 13.4,\n    \"gust_kph\": 21.6\n  },\n  \"forecast\": {\n    \"forecastday\": [\n      {\n        \"date\": \"2020-11-20\",\n        \"date_epoch\": 1605811200,\n        \"day\": {\n          \"maxtemp_c\": 12.8,\n          \"maxtemp_f\": 55,\n          \"mintemp_c\": 8.3,\n          \"mintemp_f\": 46.9,\n          \"avgtemp_c\": 10.5,\n          \"avgtemp_f\": 50.9,\n          \"maxwind_mph\": 15.3,\n          \"maxwind_kph\": 24.6,\n          \"totalprecip_mm\": 0,\n          \"totalprecip_in\": 0,\n          \"avgvis_km\": 10,\n          \"avgvis_miles\": 6.2,\n          \"avghumidity\": 65,\n          \"daily_will_it_rain\": 0,\n          \"daily_chance_of_rain\": 0,\n          \"daily_will_it_snow\": 0,\n          \"daily_chance_of_snow\": 0,\n          \"condition\": {\n            \"text\": \"Partly cloudy\",\n            \"icon\": \"//cdn.weatherapi.com/weather/128x128/day/116.png\",\n            \"code\": 1003\n          },\n          \"uv\": 2.1\n        },\n        \"astro\": {\n          \"sunrise\": \"06:50 AM\",\n          \"sunset\": \"04:28 PM\",\n          \"moonrise\": \"11:09 AM\",\n          \"moonset\": \"11:45 PM\",\n          \"moon_phase\": \"Waxing Gibbous\",\n          \"moon_illumination\": 84\n        },\n        \"hour\": [...]\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Pros:**\n- Generous free tier (1M calls/month)\n- Simple, clean API\n- Good documentation\n- Astronomy data included\n- Hourly forecast data\n- Reliable service\n\n**Cons:**\n- Smaller community compared to OpenWeatherMap\n- Limited historical data on free tier\n- Fewer advanced features\n\n---\n\n### **1.3 NOAA Weather API**\n\n**Overview:**\nNOAA (National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration) provides free, government-backed weather data primarily for the United States.\n\n**Key Features:**\n- Free weather data (US only)\n- High accuracy for US locations\n- Forecast data\n- Alerts and warnings\n- Marine forecasts\n- Fire weather forecasts\n- No API key required for basic usage\n- Comprehensive meteorological data\n\n**Pricing:**\n- Completely free\n- No rate limiting for reasonable use\n- No authentication required\n\n**API Response Example:**\n```json\n{\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"updated\": \"2020-11-20T10:00:00+00:00\",\n    \"units\": \"us\",\n    \"forecastGenerator\": \"BaseGenerator\",\n    \"generatedAt\": \"2020-11-20T10:00:00+00:00\",\n    \"updateTime\": \"2020-11-20T10:00:00+00:00\",\n    \"validTimes\": \"2020-11-20T10:00:00+00:00/P7D\",\n    \"elevation\": {\"value\": 9.1, \"unitCode\": \"wmoUnit:m\"},\n    \"periods\": [\n      {\n        \"number\": 1,\n        \"name\": \"Friday\",\n        \"startTime\": \"2020-11-20T10:00:00-05:00\",\n        \"endTime\": \"2020-11-21T00:00:00-05:00\",\n        \"isDaytime\": true,\n        \"temperature\": 49,\n        \"temperatureUnit\": \"F\",\n        \"temperatureTrend\": null,\n        \"windSpeed\": \"9 mph\",\n        \"windDirection\": \"E\",\n        \"icon\": \"https://api.weather.gov/icons/land/day/rain?size=medium\",\n        \"shortForecast\": \"Light Rain\",\n        \"detailedForecast\": \"Light rain. Cloudy. High near 49. East wind around 9 mph.\"\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Pros:**\n- Completely free\n- No rate limiting\n- High accuracy for US\n- Government-backed reliability\n- No authentication required\n- Excellent for US-focused applications\n\n**Cons:**\n- US only coverage\n- Less structured API compared to commercial alternatives\n- Requires grid point lookup first\n- Fewer advanced features\n- Smaller developer community\n\n---\n\n### **1.4 API Comparison Matrix**\n\n| Feature | OpenWeatherMap | WeatherAPI | NOAA |\n|---------|-----------------|-----------|------|\n| **Global Coverage** | Yes | Yes | US Only |\n| **Free Tier** | 1K calls/day | 1M calls/month | Unlimited |\n| **Forecast Days** | 5-16 | 10-30 | 7+ |\n| **Historical Data** | Limited free | 30 years (Pro) | Limited |\n| **Air Quality** | Yes | Yes | No |\n| **Alerts** | Yes | Yes | Yes |\n| **Hourly Data** | Limited | Yes | Yes |\n| **API Key Required** | Yes | Yes | No |\n| **Documentation** | Excellent | Good | Good |\n| **Community** | Large | Medium | Medium |\n| **SLA** | Enterprise only | No | No |\n| **Response Time** | <500ms | <500ms | <1s |\n\n**Recommendation:**\n- **Global applications**: Use OpenWeatherMap or WeatherAPI\n- **Cost-sensitive projects**: WeatherAPI (1M free calls)\n- **US-only applications**: NOAA (free, no limits)\n- **Premium services**: OpenWeatherMap (best features)\n- **Hybrid approach**: Use NOAA for US + OpenWeatherMap for international\n\n---\n\n## **2. BACKEND ARCHITECTURE AND BEST PRACTICES**\n\n### **2.1 Recommended Architecture Pattern**\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                   Client Layer                          │\n│         (Web - React/Vue, Mobile - RN/Flutter)         │\n└──────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────┘\n                       │ HTTPS/REST/GraphQL\n┌──────────────────────▼──────────────────────────────────┐\n│              API Gateway / Load Balancer                │\n│           (AWS ALB, Azure LB, GCP LB)                   │\n└──────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────┘\n                       │\n┌──────────────────────▼──────────────────────────────────┐\n│          Authentication & Authorization                 │\n│            (JWT, OAuth 2.0, API Keys)                   │\n└──────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────┘\n                       │\n    ┌──────────────────┼──────────────────┐\n    │                  │                  │\n    ▼                  ▼                  ▼\n┌─────────────┐  ┌──────────────┐  ┌──────────────┐\n│  Weather    │  │  User        │  │  Forecast    │\n│  Service    │  │  Service     │  │  Service     │\n└─────────────┘  └──────────────┘  └──────────────┘\n    │                  │                  │\n    └──────────────────┼──────────────────┘\n                       │\n    ┌──────────────────┼──────────────────┐\n    │                  │                  │\n    ▼                  ▼                  ▼\n┌─────────────┐  ┌──────────────┐  ┌──────────────┐\n│  Redis      │  │  PostgreSQL  │  │  Message    │\n│  Cache      │  │  Database    │  │  Queue      │\n└─────────────┘  └──────────────┘  └──────────────┘\n    │                  │                  │\n    └──────────────────┼──────────────────┘\n                       │\n    ┌──────────────────┼──────────────────┐\n    │                  │                  │\n    ▼                  ▼                  ▼\n┌─────────────┐  ┌──────────────┐  ┌──────────────┐\n│ External    │  │  Monitoring  │  │  Logging    │\n│ Weather API │  │  (Prometheus)│  │ (ELK Stack) │\n└─────────────┘  └──────────────┘  └──────────────┘\n```\n\n### **2.2 Backend Technology Stack Recommendations**\n\n**Option 1: Node.js/Express (Recommended for rapid development)**\n\n**Advantages:**\n- JavaScript across full stack\n- Non-blocking I/O ideal for API calls\n- Large npm ecosystem\n- Fast development cycle\n- Excellent async/await support\n\n**Key Dependencies:**\n```json\n{\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"express\": \"^4.17.1\",\n    \"axios\": \"^0.21.1\",\n    \"redis\": \"^3.1.2\",\n    \"pg\": \"^8.6.0\",\n    \"jsonwebtoken\": \"^8.5.1\",\n    \"bcryptjs\": \"^2.4.3\",\n    \"dotenv\": \"^10.0.0\",\n    \"helmet\": \"^4.6.0\",\n    \"express-rate-limit\": \"^5.3.0\",\n    \"joi\": \"^17.4.0\",\n    \"winston\": \"^3.3.3\",\n    \"cors\": \"^2.8.5\"\n  },\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"jest\": \"^27.0.6\",\n    \"supertest\": \"^6.1.3\",\n    \"nodemon\": \"^2.0.12\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Sample Express Server Structure:**\n```javascript\n// server.js\nconst express = require('express');\nconst helmet = require('helmet');\nconst cors = require('cors');\nconst rateLimit = require('express-rate-limit');\nconst authRoutes = require('./routes/auth');\nconst weatherRoutes = require('./routes/weather');\nconst userRoutes = require('./routes/users');\nconst { errorHandler } = require('./middleware/errorHandler');\nconst { logger } = require('./utils/logger');\n\nconst app = express();\n\n// Security middleware\napp.use(helmet());\napp.use(cors({\n  origin: process.env.ALLOWED_ORIGINS?.split(',') || ['http://localhost:3000'],\n  credentials: true\n}));\n\n// Rate limiting\nconst limiter = rateLimit({\n  windowMs: 15 * 60 * 1000,\n  max: 100,\n  message: 'Too many requests from this IP',\n  standardHeaders: true,\n  legacyHeaders: false,\n});\n\napp.use(limiter);\n\n// Body parsing\napp.use(express.json({ limit: '10kb' }));\napp.use(express.urlencoded({ limit: '10kb', extended: true"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "", "tool_calls": [{"id": "tooluse_51O3v1PbyzcNd6q2Y0uKp8", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "delegate_work_to_coworker", "arguments": "{\"coworker\": \"Coding Specialist\", \"task\": \"Based on the detailed weather app project plan and research provided, create a complete code outline with main components and their responsibilities. This should include the full directory structure, component descriptions, and the interconnections between all major parts of the application (both backend and frontend).\", \"context\": \"We have a comprehensive project plan for building a multi-city weather application. The key requirements are:\\n\\nBACKEND (Node.js/Express recommended):\\n- Authentication module with JWT tokens\\n- Weather API integration (OpenWeatherMap, WeatherAPI, or NOAA)\\n- Database schema with Users, Cities, User_Cities, Weather_Cache, API_Logs entities\\n- RESTful API endpoints for weather data, user management, favorites\\n- Caching strategy (1-hour TTL for current weather, 6-hour for forecast)\\n- Rate limiting and error handling\\n- Logging and monitoring\\n\\nFRONTEND (React/Vue recommended):\\n- Login/Registration screens\\n- Dashboard with multiple cities weather display\\n- Detailed weather forecast screen (7-day)\\n- City search and add functionality\\n- User settings/preferences\\n- Favorites management\\n- Responsive design with dark mode support\\n- State management (Redux/Zustand/Context API)\\n- API service layer with interceptors\\n\\nKEY COMPONENTS TO INCLUDE:\\n1. Authentication service\\n2. Weather data integration module\\n3. User management module\\n4. City management module\\n5. Caching layer\\n6. Database models\\n7. API routes\\n8. Frontend components\\n9. State management\\n10. Error handling and logging\\n\\nThe outline should show the complete file structure, describe each component's responsibility, and explain how they interact with each other. Return the actual complete content, not a summary.\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "content": "# Complete Weather App Project Code Outline\n\n## Project Structure Overview\n\n```\nweather-app/\n├── backend/\n│   ├── src/\n│   │   ├── config/\n│   │   │   ├── database.js\n│   │   │   ├── environment.js\n│   │   │   └── cache.js\n│   │   ├── middleware/\n│   │   │   ├── authentication.js\n│   │   │   ├── errorHandler.js\n│   │   │   ├── rateLimiter.js\n│   │   │   └── logger.js\n│   │   ├── models/\n│   │   │   ├── User.js\n│   │   │   ├── City.js\n│   │   │   ├── UserCity.js\n│   │   │   ├── WeatherCache.js\n│   │   │   └── APILog.js\n│   │   ├── services/\n│   │   │   ├── AuthService.js\n│   │   │   ├── WeatherService.js\n│   │   │   ├── UserService.js\n│   │   │   ├── CityService.js\n│   │   │   ├── CacheService.js\n│   │   │   └── ExternalWeatherAPI.js\n│   │   ├── routes/\n│   │   │   ├── authRoutes.js\n│   │   │   ├── weatherRoutes.js\n│   │   │   ├── userRoutes.js\n│   │   │   ├── cityRoutes.js\n│   │   │   └── index.js\n│   │   ├── controllers/\n│   │   │   ├── AuthController.js\n│   │   │   ├── WeatherController.js\n│   │   │   ├── UserController.js\n│   │   │   └── CityController.js\n│   │   ├── utils/\n│   │   │   ├── validators.js\n│   │   │   ├── errorFormatter.js\n│   │   │   ├── tokenGenerator.js\n│   │   │   └── weatherDataMapper.js\n│   │   ├── app.js\n│   │   └── server.js\n│   ├── tests/\n│   │   ├── unit/\n│   │   ├── integration/\n│   │   └── fixtures/\n│   ├── .env.example\n│   ├── .gitignore\n│   ├── package.json\n│   └── README.md\n│\n├── frontend/\n│   ├── public/\n│   │   ├── index.html\n│   │   ├── favicon.ico\n│   │   └── manifest.json\n│   ├── src/\n│   │   ├── components/\n│   │   │   ├── Auth/\n│   │   │   │   ├── LoginForm.jsx\n│   │   │   │   ├── RegisterForm.jsx\n│   │   │   │   ├── ProtectedRoute.jsx\n│   │   │   │   └── AuthLayout.jsx\n│   │   │   ├── Dashboard/\n│   │   │   │   ├── Dashboard.jsx\n│   │   │   │   ├── WeatherCard.jsx\n│   │   │   │   ├── CityGrid.jsx\n│   │   │   │   ├── AddCityModal.jsx\n│   │   │   │   └── FavoritesSection.jsx\n│   │   │   ├── Weather/\n│   │   │   │   ├── WeatherDetail.jsx\n│   │   │   │   ├── ForecastView.jsx\n│   │   │   │   ├── ForecastCard.jsx\n│   │   │   │   ├── CurrentWeatherDisplay.jsx\n│   │   │   │   └── WeatherMetrics.jsx\n│   │   │   ├── Search/\n│   │   │   │   ├── CitySearch.jsx\n│   │   │   │   ├── SearchResults.jsx\n│   │   │   │   └── SearchBar.jsx\n│   │   │   ├── Settings/\n│   │   │   │   ├── SettingsPage.jsx\n│   │   │   │   ├── PreferencesForm.jsx\n│   │   │   │   ├── ThemeToggle.jsx\n│   │   │   │   └── UnitsSelector.jsx\n│   │   │   ├── Common/\n│   │   │   │   ├── Header.jsx\n│   │   │   │   ├── Sidebar.jsx\n│   │   │   │   ├── LoadingSpinner.jsx\n│   │   │   │   ├── ErrorBoundary.jsx\n│   │   │   │   ├── Notification.jsx\n│   │   │   │   └── Footer.jsx\n│   │   │   └── Layout/\n│   │   │       ├── MainLayout.jsx\n│   │   │       └── AppContainer.jsx\n│   │   ├── pages/\n│   │   │   ├── LoginPage.jsx\n│   │   │   ├── RegisterPage.jsx\n│   │   │   ├── DashboardPage.jsx\n│   │   │   ├── WeatherDetailPage.jsx\n│   │   │   ├── SettingsPage.jsx\n│   │   │   ├── NotFoundPage.jsx\n│   │   │   └── ErrorPage.jsx\n│   │   ├── store/\n│   │   │   ├── index.js\n│   │   │   ├── slices/\n│   │   │   │   ├── authSlice.js\n│   │   │   │   ├── weatherSlice.js\n│   │   │   │   ├── userSlice.js\n│   │   │   │   ├── citySlice.js\n│   │   │   │   ├── uiSlice.js\n│   │   │   │   └── settingsSlice.js\n│   │   │   ├── selectors/\n│   │   │   │   ├── authSelectors.js\n│   │   │   │   ├── weatherSelectors.js\n│   │   │   │   ├── citySelectors.js\n│   │   │   │   └── settingsSelectors.js\n│   │   │   └── thunks/\n│   │   │       ├── authThunks.js\n│   │   │       ├── weatherThunks.js\n│   │   │       ├── userThunks.js\n│   │   │       └── cityThunks.js\n│   │   ├── services/\n│   │   │   ├── api/\n│   │   │   │   ├── axiosInstance.js\n│   │   │   │   ├── apiClient.js\n│   │   │   │   ├── endpoints.js\n│   │   │   │   └── interceptors.js\n│   │   │   ├── auth/\n│   │   │   │   ├── AuthService.js\n│   │   │   │   └── TokenService.js\n│   │   │   ├── weather/\n│   │   │   │   ├── WeatherService.js\n│   │   │   │   └── ForecastService.js\n│   │   │   ├── user/\n│   │   │   │   └── UserService.js\n│   │   │   └── city/\n│   │   │       └── CityService.js\n│   │   ├── hooks/\n│   │   │   ├── useAuth.js\n│   │   │   ├── useWeather.js\n│   │   │   ├── useCity.js\n│   │   │   ├── useSettings.js\n│   │   │   ├── useLocalStorage.js\n│   │   │   └── useFetch.js\n│   │   ├── styles/\n│   │   │   ├── index.css\n│   │   │   ├── variables.css\n│   │   │   ├── theme.css\n│   │   │   ├── responsive.css\n│   │   │   └── components/\n│   │   │       ├── auth.css\n│   │   │       ├── dashboard.css\n│   │   │       ├── weather.css\n│   │   │       ├── settings.css\n│   │   │       └── common.css\n│   │   ├── utils/\n│   │   │   ├── formatters.js\n│   │   │   ├── validators.js\n│   │   │   ├── constants.js\n│   │   │   ├── helpers.js\n│   │   │   └── errorHandler.js\n│   │   ├── config/\n│   │   │   ├── apiConfig.js\n│   │   │   ├── appConfig.js\n│   │   │   └── constants.js\n│   │   ├── App.jsx\n│   │   ├── index.jsx\n│   │   └── setupTests.js\n│   ├── tests/\n│   │   ├── unit/\n│   │   ├── integration/\n│   │   └── fixtures/\n│   ├── .env.example\n│   ├── .gitignore\n│   ├── package.json\n│   ├── vite.config.js\n│   └── README.md\n│\n├── docker-compose.yml\n├── .gitignore\n└── README.md\n```\n\n---\n\n## BACKEND DETAILED COMPONENT DESCRIPTIONS\n\n### 1. Configuration Layer (`backend/src/config/`)\n\n#### `database.js`\n```javascript\n/**\n * DATABASE CONFIGURATION\n * Responsibility: Initialize and configure database connection\n * \n * Features:\n * - PostgreSQL/MySQL connection pooling\n * - Connection retry logic\n * - Database migration runner\n * - Connection health checks\n */\n\nconst { Pool } = require('pg');\nconst fs = require('fs');\nconst path = require('path');\n\nclass DatabaseConfig {\n  constructor() {\n    this.pool = null;\n    this.isConnected = false;\n  }\n\n  async initialize() {\n    this.pool = new Pool({\n      user: process.env.DB_USER,\n      password: process.env.DB_PASSWORD,\n      host: process.env.DB_HOST,\n      port: process.env.DB_PORT,\n      database: process.env.DB_NAME,\n      max: 20,\n      idleTimeoutMillis: 30000,\n      connectionTimeoutMillis: 2000,\n    });\n\n    this.pool.on('error', (err) => {\n      console.error('Unexpected pool error:', err);\n    });\n\n    try {\n      await this.pool.query('SELECT NOW()');\n      this.isConnected = true;\n      console.log('Database connected successfully');\n    } catch (err) {\n      console.error('Database connection failed:', err);\n      throw err;\n    }\n  }\n\n  async runMigrations() {\n    // Read and execute migration files\n  }\n\n  async query(text, params) {\n    return this.pool.query(text, params);\n  }\n\n  async getConnection() {\n    return this.pool.connect();\n  }\n\n  async close() {\n    await this.pool.end();\n    this.isConnected = false;\n  }\n\n  isHealthy() {\n    return this.isConnected;\n  }\n}\n\nmodule.exports = new DatabaseConfig();\n```\n\n#### `cache.js`\n```javascript\n/**\n * CACHE CONFIGURATION\n * Responsibility: Redis cache initialization and configuration\n * \n * Features:\n * - Redis connection management\n * - TTL configuration for different data types\n * - Cache key naming conventions\n * - Connection pooling and error handling\n */\n\nconst redis = require('redis');\n\nclass CacheConfig {\n  constructor() {\n    this.client = null;\n    this.isConnected = false;\n    this.TTL = {\n      CURRENT_WEATHER: 3600, // 1 hour\n      FORECAST_WEATHER: 21600, // 6 hours\n      USER_PREFERENCES: 86400, // 24 hours\n      CITY_LIST: 43200, // 12 hours\n    };\n  }\n\n  async initialize() {\n    this.client = redis.createClient({\n      host: process.env.REDIS_HOST || 'localhost',\n      port: process.env.REDIS_PORT || 6379,\n      password: process.env.REDIS_PASSWORD,\n      retryStrategy: (times) => Math.min(times * 50, 2000),\n    });\n\n    this.client.on('error', (err) => {\n      console.error('Redis error:', err);\n    });\n\n    this.client.on('connect', () => {\n      this.isConnected = true;\n      console.log('Redis connected');\n    });\n\n    return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {\n      this.client.on('ready', resolve);\n      this.client.on('error', reject);\n    });\n  }\n\n  async get(key) {\n    return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {\n      this.client.get(key, (err, data) => {\n        if (err) reject(err);\n        resolve(data ? JSON.parse(data) : null);\n      });\n    });\n  }\n\n  async set(key, value, ttl = this.TTL.CURRENT_WEATHER) {\n    return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {\n      this.client.setex(key, ttl, JSON.stringify(value), (err) => {\n        if (err) reject(err);\n        resolve();\n      });\n    });\n  }\n\n  async delete(key) {\n    return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {\n      this.client.del(key, (err) => {\n        if (err) reject(err);\n        resolve();\n      });\n    });\n  }\n\n  async flush() {\n    return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {\n      this.client.flushdb((err) => {\n        if (err) reject(err);\n        resolve();\n      });\n    });\n  }\n\n  isHealthy() {\n    return this.isConnected;\n  }\n}\n\nmodule.exports = new CacheConfig();\n```\n\n#### `environment.js`\n```javascript\n/**\n * ENVIRONMENT CONFIGURATION\n * Responsibility: Load and validate environment variables\n * \n * Features:\n * - Environment variable validation\n * - Default value assignment\n * - Configuration object creation\n * - Environment-specific settings\n */\n\nrequire('dotenv').config();\n\nconst config = {\n  // Server Configuration\n  NODE_ENV: process.env.NODE_ENV || 'development',\n  PORT: process.env.PORT || 5000,\n  HOST: process.env.HOST || 'localhost',\n\n  // Database Configuration\n  DB_HOST: process.env.DB_HOST,\n  DB_PORT: process.env.DB_PORT || 5432,\n  DB_USER: process.env.DB_USER,\n  DB_PASSWORD: process.env.DB_PASSWORD,\n  DB_NAME: process.env.DB_NAME,\n\n  // Redis Configuration\n  REDIS_HOST: process.env.REDIS_HOST || 'localhost',\n  REDIS_PORT: process.env.REDIS_PORT || 6379,\n  REDIS_PASSWORD: process.env.REDIS_PASSWORD,\n\n  // JWT Configuration\n  JWT_SECRET: process.env.JWT_SECRET,\n  JWT_EXPIRY: process.env.JWT_EXPIRY || '7d',\n  REFRESH_TOKEN_SECRET: process.env.REFRESH_TOKEN_SECRET,\n\n  // Weather API Configuration\n  WEATHER_API_PROVIDER: process.env.WEATHER_API_PROVIDER || 'openweathermap',\n  OPENWEATHERMAP_API_KEY: process.env.OPENWEATHERMAP_API_KEY,\n  WEATHERAPI_API_KEY: process.env.WEATHERAPI_API_KEY,\n  NOAA_BASE_URL: process.env.NOAA_BASE_URL,\n\n  // Rate Limiting\n  RATE_LIMIT_WINDOW_MS: parseInt(process.env.RATE_LIMIT_WINDOW_MS) || 900000,\n  RATE_LIMIT_MAX_REQUESTS: parseInt(process.env.RATE_LIMIT_MAX_REQUESTS) || ", "tool_call_id": "tooluse_51O3v1PbyzcNd6q2Y0uKp8", "name": "delegate_work_to_coworker"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "", "tool_calls": [{"id": "tooluse_fB4GGNcztRo55XBbkBf6q5", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "ask_question_to_coworker", "arguments": "{\"context\": \"We've started receiving a detailed code outline for the weather app. The outline shows the complete file structure and is beginning to detail the backend components including configuration layer (database.js, cache.js, environment.js). We need the complete and full content of all remaining components including:\\n\\n1. Middleware layer (authentication, error handling, rate limiting, logging)\\n2. Models/Database schemas (User, City, UserCity, WeatherCache, APILog)\\n3. Services layer (Auth, Weather, User, City, Cache, ExternalWeatherAPI)\\n4. Controllers layer\\n5. Routes layer\\n6. Frontend components and services\\n7. State management (Redux slices, thunks, selectors)\\n8. Hooks and utilities\\n\\nThe user explicitly requested the ACTUAL COMPLETE CONTENT as the final answer, not a summary.\", \"coworker\": \"Coding Specialist\", \"question\": \"Please provide the complete, full code outline for the weather app including all remaining backend components (middleware, models, services, controllers, routes) and all frontend components (components, pages, store, services, hooks). This should be the actual complete content with full descriptions and code examples for each component, not a summary.\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "content": "# Complete Weather App Code Outline - Full Implementation\n\nI'll provide the complete, full code content for all remaining backend and frontend components.\n\n---\n\n## BACKEND STRUCTURE\n\n### 1. MIDDLEWARE LAYER\n\n#### `src/middleware/auth.middleware.js`\n```javascript\nconst jwt = require('jsonwebtoken');\nconst { AppError } = require('../utils/errors');\nconst { logger } = require('../config/logger');\n\n/**\n * Authentication middleware to verify JWT tokens\n * Extracts and validates token from Authorization header\n * Attaches user data to request object\n */\nconst authMiddleware = (req, res, next) => {\n  try {\n    const authHeader = req.headers.authorization;\n    \n    if (!authHeader || !authHeader.startsWith('Bearer ')) {\n      return next(new AppError('No token provided', 401));\n    }\n\n    const token = authHeader.substring(7);\n    \n    try {\n      const decoded = jwt.verify(token, process.env.JWT_SECRET);\n      req.user = decoded;\n      next();\n    } catch (error) {\n      if (error.name === 'TokenExpiredError') {\n        return next(new AppError('Token expired', 401));\n      }\n      if (error.name === 'JsonWebTokenError') {\n        return next(new AppError('Invalid token', 401));\n      }\n      throw error;\n    }\n  } catch (error) {\n    logger.error('Auth middleware error:', error);\n    next(new AppError('Authentication failed', 500));\n  }\n};\n\n/**\n * Optional authentication middleware\n * Attempts to authenticate but doesn't fail if no token\n */\nconst optionalAuthMiddleware = (req, res, next) => {\n  try {\n    const authHeader = req.headers.authorization;\n    \n    if (authHeader && authHeader.startsWith('Bearer ')) {\n      const token = authHeader.substring(7);\n      try {\n        const decoded = jwt.verify(token, process.env.JWT_SECRET);\n        req.user = decoded;\n      } catch (error) {\n        logger.warn('Optional auth token validation failed:', error.message);\n        // Continue without user data\n      }\n    }\n    next();\n  } catch (error) {\n    logger.error('Optional auth middleware error:', error);\n    next();\n  }\n};\n\n/**\n * Role-based access control middleware\n * Verifies user has required role\n */\nconst roleMiddleware = (allowedRoles = []) => {\n  return (req, res, next) => {\n    if (!req.user) {\n      return next(new AppError('User not authenticated', 401));\n    }\n\n    if (!allowedRoles.includes(req.user.role)) {\n      return next(new AppError('Insufficient permissions', 403));\n    }\n\n    next();\n  };\n};\n\nmodule.exports = {\n  authMiddleware,\n  optionalAuthMiddleware,\n  roleMiddleware\n};\n```\n\n#### `src/middleware/errorHandler.middleware.js`\n```javascript\nconst { logger } = require('../config/logger');\nconst { AppError } = require('../utils/errors');\n\n/**\n * Global error handling middleware\n * Catches all errors and formats response\n * Logs errors based on severity\n */\nconst errorHandlerMiddleware = (err, req, res, next) => {\n  // Default error values\n  let error = { ...err };\n  error.message = err.message;\n\n  // Log error details\n  logger.error(`Error: ${err.message}`, {\n    statusCode: error.statusCode || 500,\n    path: req.path,\n    method: req.method,\n    stack: err.stack,\n    userId: req.user?.id\n  });\n\n  // Handle AppError instances\n  if (err instanceof AppError) {\n    const { statusCode, message } = err;\n    return res.status(statusCode).json({\n      success: false,\n      error: {\n        message,\n        statusCode\n      }\n    });\n  }\n\n  // Handle JWT errors\n  if (err.name === 'JsonWebTokenError') {\n    return res.status(401).json({\n      success: false,\n      error: {\n        message: 'Invalid token',\n        statusCode: 401\n      }\n    });\n  }\n\n  if (err.name === 'TokenExpiredError') {\n    return res.status(401).json({\n      success: false,\n      error: {\n        message: 'Token expired',\n        statusCode: 401\n      }\n    });\n  }\n\n  // Handle Mongoose validation errors\n  if (err.name === 'ValidationError') {\n    const messages = Object.values(err.errors).map(e => e.message);\n    return res.status(400).json({\n      success: false,\n      error: {\n        message: 'Validation error',\n        details: messages,\n        statusCode: 400\n      }\n    });\n  }\n\n  // Handle Mongoose duplicate key errors\n  if (err.code === 11000) {\n    const field = Object.keys(err.keyPattern)[0];\n    return res.status(409).json({\n      success: false,\n      error: {\n        message: `${field} already exists`,\n        statusCode: 409\n      }\n    });\n  }\n\n  // Handle Cast errors\n  if (err.name === 'CastError') {\n    return res.status(400).json({\n      success: false,\n      error: {\n        message: 'Invalid ID format',\n        statusCode: 400\n      }\n    });\n  }\n\n  // Default server error\n  res.status(error.statusCode || 500).json({\n    success: false,\n    error: {\n      message: error.message || 'Internal server error',\n      statusCode: error.statusCode || 500\n    }\n  });\n};\n\n/**\n * Async error wrapper for route handlers\n * Catches errors and passes to error handler\n */\nconst asyncHandler = (fn) => (req, res, next) => {\n  Promise.resolve(fn(req, res, next)).catch(next);\n};\n\nmodule.exports = {\n  errorHandlerMiddleware,\n  asyncHandler\n};\n```\n\n#### `src/middleware/rateLimiter.middleware.js`\n```javascript\nconst rateLimit = require('express-rate-limit');\nconst RedisStore = require('rate-limit-redis');\nconst { redisClient } = require('../config/cache');\nconst { AppError } = require('../utils/errors');\n\n/**\n * General API rate limiter\n * 100 requests per 15 minutes per IP\n */\nconst generalLimiter = rateLimit({\n  store: new RedisStore({\n    client: redisClient,\n    prefix: 'rate-limit:general:'\n  }),\n  windowMs: 15 * 60 * 1000, // 15 minutes\n  max: 100,\n  message: 'Too many requests from this IP, please try again later.',\n  standardHeaders: true,\n  legacyHeaders: false,\n  handler: (req, res) => {\n    throw new AppError('Too many requests', 429);\n  }\n});\n\n/**\n * Authentication rate limiter\n * 5 requests per 15 minutes per IP\n * Prevents brute force attacks\n */\nconst authLimiter = rateLimit({\n  store: new RedisStore({\n    client: redisClient,\n    prefix: 'rate-limit:auth:'\n  }),\n  windowMs: 15 * 60 * 1000,\n  max: 5,\n  message: 'Too many login attempts, please try again later.',\n  skipSuccessfulRequests: true,\n  handler: (req, res) => {\n    throw new AppError('Too many login attempts', 429);\n  }\n});\n\n/**\n * Weather API rate limiter\n * 50 requests per minute per user\n * Prevents excessive API usage\n */\nconst weatherLimiter = rateLimit({\n  store: new RedisStore({\n    client: redisClient,\n    prefix: 'rate-limit:weather:'\n  }),\n  windowMs: 60 * 1000, // 1 minute\n  max: 50,\n  keyGenerator: (req) => {\n    return req.user?.id || req.ip;\n  },\n  message: 'Too many weather requests, please try again later.',\n  handler: (req, res) => {\n    throw new AppError('Weather API rate limit exceeded', 429);\n  }\n});\n\n/**\n * Search rate limiter\n * 30 requests per minute per user\n */\nconst searchLimiter = rateLimit({\n  store: new RedisStore({\n    client: redisClient,\n    prefix: 'rate-limit:search:'\n  }),\n  windowMs: 60 * 1000,\n  max: 30,\n  keyGenerator: (req) => {\n    return req.user?.id || req.ip;\n  }\n});\n\nmodule.exports = {\n  generalLimiter,\n  authLimiter,\n  weatherLimiter,\n  searchLimiter\n};\n```\n\n#### `src/middleware/logging.middleware.js`\n```javascript\nconst { logger } = require('../config/logger');\n\n/**\n * HTTP request logging middleware\n * Logs all incoming requests with method, path, and response time\n */\nconst requestLoggingMiddleware = (req, res, next) => {\n  const startTime = Date.now();\n  \n  // Capture response data\n  const originalSend = res.send;\n  res.send = function(data) {\n    const duration = Date.now() - startTime;\n    const statusCode = res.statusCode;\n    \n    logger.info(`${req.method} ${req.path}`, {\n      statusCode,\n      duration: `${duration}ms`,\n      ip: req.ip,\n      userId: req.user?.id,\n      userAgent: req.get('user-agent')\n    });\n\n    // Call original send\n    return originalSend.call(this, data);\n  };\n\n  next();\n};\n\n/**\n * Request sanitization middleware\n * Removes sensitive data from logs\n */\nconst sanitizeLogsMiddleware = (req, res, next) => {\n  const sensitiveFields = ['password', 'token', 'apiKey', 'secret'];\n  \n  const sanitizeObject = (obj) => {\n    const sanitized = { ...obj };\n    sensitiveFields.forEach(field => {\n      if (sanitized[field]) {\n        sanitized[field] = '***REDACTED***';\n      }\n    });\n    return sanitized;\n  };\n\n  // Sanitize request body and query\n  if (req.body) {\n    req.body = sanitizeObject(req.body);\n  }\n  if (req.query) {\n    req.query = sanitizeObject(req.query);\n  }\n\n  next();\n};\n\n/**\n * Request correlation ID middleware\n * Adds unique ID to each request for tracing\n */\nconst correlationIdMiddleware = (req, res, next) => {\n  const correlationId = req.get('x-correlation-id') || \n    `${Date.now()}-${Math.random().toString(36).substr(2, 9)}`;\n  \n  req.correlationId = correlationId;\n  res.set('x-correlation-id', correlationId);\n  \n  next();\n};\n\nmodule.exports = {\n  requestLoggingMiddleware,\n  sanitizeLogsMiddleware,\n  correlationIdMiddleware\n};\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. MODELS/DATABASE SCHEMAS\n\n#### `src/models/User.js`\n```javascript\nconst mongoose = require('mongoose');\nconst bcrypt = require('bcryptjs');\nconst { logger } = require('../config/logger');\n\nconst userSchema = new mongoose.Schema(\n  {\n    username: {\n      type: String,\n      required: [true, 'Username is required'],\n      unique: true,\n      trim: true,\n      minlength: [3, 'Username must be at least 3 characters'],\n      maxlength: [30, 'Username cannot exceed 30 characters'],\n      match: [/^[a-zA-Z0-9_-]+$/, 'Username can only contain letters, numbers, underscore, and hyphen']\n    },\n    email: {\n      type: String,\n      required: [true, 'Email is required'],\n      unique: true,\n      lowercase: true,\n      match: [/^\\w+([\\.-]?\\w+)*@\\w+([\\.-]?\\w+)*(\\.\\w{2,3})+$/, 'Please provide a valid email']\n    },\n    password: {\n      type: String,\n      required: [true, 'Password is required'],\n      minlength: [6, 'Password must be at least 6 characters'],\n      select: false // Don't include password by default in queries\n    },\n    firstName: {\n      type: String,\n      trim: true\n    },\n    lastName: {\n      type: String,\n      trim: true\n    },\n    avatar: {\n      type: String,\n      default: null\n    },\n    role: {\n      type: String,\n      enum: ['user', 'admin'],\n      default: 'user'\n    },\n    isEmailVerified: {\n      type: Boolean,\n      default: false\n    },\n    emailVerificationToken: {\n      type: String,\n      select: false\n    },\n    emailVerificationExpires: {\n      type: Date,\n      select: false\n    },\n    passwordResetToken: {\n      type: String,\n      select: false\n    },\n    passwordResetExpires: {\n      type: Date,\n      select: false\n    },\n    lastLogin: {\n      type: Date,\n      default: null\n    },\n    loginAttempts: {\n      type: Number,\n      default: 0\n    },\n    lockUntil: {\n      type: Date,\n      default: null\n    },\n    preferences: {\n      temperatureUnit: {\n        type: String,\n        enum: ['celsius', 'fahrenheit'],\n        default: 'celsius'\n      },\n      windSpeedUnit: {\n        type: String,\n        enum: ['ms', 'kmh', 'mph'],\n        default: 'kmh'\n      },\n      theme: {\n        type: String,\n        enum: ['light', 'dark'],\n        default: 'light'\n      },\n      notificationsEnabled: {\n        type: Boolean,\n        default: true\n      },\n      emailNotifications: {\n        type: Boolean,\n        default: false\n      }\n    },\n    isActive: {\n      type: Boolean,\n      default: true\n    },\n    deletedAt: {\n      type: Date,\n      default: null\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    timestamps: true,\n    toJSON: { virtuals: true },\n    toObject: { virtuals: true }\n  }\n);\n\n// Virtual for full name\nuserSchema.virtual('fullName').get(function() {\n  return `${this.firstName || ''} ${this.lastName || ''}`.trim();\n});\n\n// Hash password before saving\nuserSchema.pre('save', async function(next) {\n  if (!this.isModified('password')) return next();\n\n  try {\n    const salt = await bcrypt.genSalt(10);\n    this.password = await bcrypt.hash(this.password, salt);\n    next();\n  } catch (error) {\n    logger.error('Error hashing password:', error);\n    next(error);\n  }\n});\n\n// Method to compare passwords\nuserSchema.methods.comparePassword = async function(enteredPassword) {\n  return await bcrypt.compare(enteredPassword, this.password);\n};\n\n// Method to check if account is locked\nuserSchema.methods.isAccountLocked = function() {\n  return this.lockUntil && this.lockUntil > Date.now();\n};\n\n// Method to increment login attempts\nuserSchema.methods.incLoginAttempts = async function() {\n  // Reset attempts if lock has expired\n  if (this.lockUntil && this.lockUntil < Date.now()) {\n    return this.updateOne({\n      $set: { loginAttempts: 1 },\n      $unset: { lockUntil: 1 }\n    });\n  }\n\n  // Increment attempts and lock if necessary\n  const updates = { $inc: { loginAttempts: 1 } };\n  const maxAttempts = 5;\n  const lockTime = 2 * 60 * 60 * 1000; // 2 hours\n\n  if (this.login", "tool_call_id": "tooluse_fB4GGNcztRo55XBbkBf6q5", "name": "ask_question_to_coworker"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "", "tool_calls": [{"id": "tooluse_nj85BN6QhdWmE7IyacaVSn", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "delegate_work_to_coworker", "arguments": "{\"context\": \"We're building the complete code outline for the weather app. We have started with middleware layer. We need the complete continuation including:\\n\\nREMAINING BACKEND COMPONENTS:\\n1. Complete Models (User, City, UserCity, WeatherCache, APILog with all methods and validations)\\n2. Services Layer (AuthService, WeatherService, UserService, CityService, CacheService, ExternalWeatherAPI with full implementation)\\n3. Controllers Layer (AuthController, WeatherController, UserController, CityController with all endpoints)\\n4. Routes Layer (all route definitions with middleware)\\n5. Utils (validators, errorFormatter, tokenGenerator, weatherDataMapper)\\n\\nFRONTEND COMPONENTS:\\n1. Auth Components (LoginForm, RegisterForm, ProtectedRoute)\\n2. Dashboard Components (Dashboard, WeatherCard, CityGrid, AddCityModal)\\n3. Weather Components (WeatherDetail, ForecastView, CurrentWeatherDisplay)\\n4. Search Components (CitySearch, SearchResults)\\n5. Settings Components (SettingsPage, PreferencesForm, ThemeToggle)\\n6. Common Components (Header, Sidebar, LoadingSpinner, ErrorBoundary)\\n\\nSTATE MANAGEMENT:\\n1. Redux slices (authSlice, weatherSlice, userSlice, citySlice, uiSlice, settingsSlice)\\n2. Thunks for async operations\\n3. Selectors\\n4. Store configuration\\n\\nSERVICES & HOOKS:\\n1. API Client with interceptors\\n2. Auth Service\\n3. Weather Service\\n4. Custom hooks (useAuth, useWeather, useCity, useSettings, useFetch)\\n\\nProvide the complete, actual code content for ALL of these components with full implementations, not summaries.\", \"coworker\": \"Coding Specialist\", \"task\": \"Provide the COMPLETE implementation of ALL remaining backend and frontend components for the weather app. This must include the actual full code content for: all Models (User, City, UserCity, WeatherCache, APILog), all Services (Auth, Weather, User, City, Cache, ExternalWeatherAPI), all Controllers, all Routes, all Utils, all Frontend Components, all Redux slices/thunks/selectors, all Services (API, Auth, Weather, User, City), and all Custom Hooks. Return the complete actual code, not summaries.\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "content": "# COMPLETE WEATHER APP IMPLEMENTATION\n\nI'll provide the complete, actual code for all backend and frontend components.\n\n## BACKEND IMPLEMENTATION\n\n### 1. MODELS\n\n#### User Model\n```javascript\n// backend/models/User.js\nconst mongoose = require('mongoose');\nconst bcrypt = require('bcryptjs');\nconst validator = require('validator');\n\nconst userSchema = new mongoose.Schema(\n  {\n    username: {\n      type: String,\n      required: [true, 'Please provide a username'],\n      unique: true,\n      trim: true,\n      minlength: [3, 'Username must be at least 3 characters'],\n      maxlength: [30, 'Username must not exceed 30 characters'],\n      match: [/^[a-zA-Z0-9_-]+$/, 'Username can only contain letters, numbers, underscores, and hyphens'],\n    },\n    email: {\n      type: String,\n      required: [true, 'Please provide an email'],\n      unique: true,\n      lowercase: true,\n      validate: [validator.isEmail, 'Please provide a valid email'],\n    },\n    password: {\n      type: String,\n      required: [true, 'Please provide a password'],\n      minlength: [6, 'Password must be at least 6 characters'],\n      select: false,\n    },\n    firstName: {\n      type: String,\n      trim: true,\n      maxlength: [50, 'First name must not exceed 50 characters'],\n    },\n    lastName: {\n      type: String,\n      trim: true,\n      maxlength: [50, 'Last name must not exceed 50 characters'],\n    },\n    profileImage: {\n      type: String,\n      default: null,\n    },\n    bio: {\n      type: String,\n      maxlength: [500, 'Bio must not exceed 500 characters'],\n    },\n    preferences: {\n      temperatureUnit: {\n        type: String,\n        enum: ['celsius', 'fahrenheit', 'kelvin'],\n        default: 'celsius',\n      },\n      windSpeedUnit: {\n        type: String,\n        enum: ['ms', 'kmh', 'mph', 'knots'],\n        default: 'ms',\n      },\n      theme: {\n        type: String,\n        enum: ['light', 'dark', 'auto'],\n        default: 'auto',\n      },\n      language: {\n        type: String,\n        default: 'en',\n      },\n      notificationsEnabled: {\n        type: Boolean,\n        default: true,\n      },\n      emailNotifications: {\n        type: Boolean,\n        default: false,\n      },\n    },\n    isEmailVerified: {\n      type: Boolean,\n      default: false,\n    },\n    emailVerificationToken: {\n      type: String,\n      select: false,\n    },\n    emailVerificationExpires: Date,\n    passwordResetToken: {\n      type: String,\n      select: false,\n    },\n    passwordResetExpires: Date,\n    lastLogin: Date,\n    loginAttempts: {\n      type: Number,\n      default: 0,\n    },\n    lockUntil: Date,\n    isActive: {\n      type: Boolean,\n      default: true,\n    },\n    role: {\n      type: String,\n      enum: ['user', 'admin'],\n      default: 'user',\n    },\n  },\n  {\n    timestamps: true,\n  }\n);\n\n// Hash password before saving\nuserSchema.pre('save', async function (next) {\n  if (!this.isModified('password')) return next();\n\n  try {\n    const salt = await bcrypt.genSalt(10);\n    this.password = await bcrypt.hash(this.password, salt);\n    next();\n  } catch (error) {\n    next(error);\n  }\n});\n\n// Instance methods\nuserSchema.methods.comparePassword = async function (enteredPassword) {\n  return await bcrypt.compare(enteredPassword, this.password);\n};\n\nuserSchema.methods.isLocked = function () {\n  return this.lockUntil && this.lockUntil > Date.now();\n};\n\nuserSchema.methods.incLoginAttempts = async function () {\n  if (this.lockUntil && this.lockUntil < Date.now()) {\n    return this.updateOne({\n      $set: { loginAttempts: 1 },\n      $unset: { lockUntil: 1 },\n    });\n  }\n\n  const updates = { $inc: { loginAttempts: 1 } };\n\n  const maxAttempts = 5;\n  const lockTime = 2 * 60 * 60 * 1000; // 2 hours\n\n  if (this.loginAttempts + 1 >= maxAttempts && !this.isLocked()) {\n    updates.$set = { lockUntil: Date.now() + lockTime };\n  }\n\n  return this.updateOne(updates);\n};\n\nuserSchema.methods.resetLoginAttempts = async function () {\n  return this.updateOne({\n    $set: { loginAttempts: 0 },\n    $unset: { lockUntil: 1 },\n  });\n};\n\nuserSchema.methods.createPasswordResetToken = function () {\n  const crypto = require('crypto');\n  const resetToken = crypto.randomBytes(32).toString('hex');\n  this.passwordResetToken = crypto\n    .createHash('sha256')\n    .update(resetToken)\n    .digest('hex');\n  this.passwordResetExpires = Date.now() + 10 * 60 * 1000; // 10 minutes\n\n  return resetToken;\n};\n\nuserSchema.methods.createEmailVerificationToken = function () {\n  const crypto = require('crypto');\n  const verificationToken = crypto.randomBytes(32).toString('hex');\n  this.emailVerificationToken = crypto\n    .createHash('sha256')\n    .update(verificationToken)\n    .digest('hex');\n  this.emailVerificationExpires = Date.now() + 24 * 60 * 60 * 1000; // 24 hours\n\n  return verificationToken;\n};\n\nuserSchema.methods.toJSON = function () {\n  const user = this.toObject();\n  delete user.password;\n  delete user.passwordResetToken;\n  delete user.emailVerificationToken;\n  delete user.loginAttempts;\n  delete user.lockUntil;\n  return user;\n};\n\n// Statics\nuserSchema.statics.findByCredentials = async function (email, password) {\n  const user = await this.findOne({ email }).select('+password');\n\n  if (!user) {\n    throw new Error('Unable to login');\n  }\n\n  if (user.isLocked()) {\n    throw new Error('Account is locked. Please try again later.');\n  }\n\n  const isPasswordMatch = await user.comparePassword(password);\n\n  if (!isPasswordMatch) {\n    await user.incLoginAttempts();\n    throw new Error('Unable to login');\n  }\n\n  await user.resetLoginAttempts();\n  return user;\n};\n\nmodule.exports = mongoose.model('User', userSchema);\n```\n\n#### City Model\n```javascript\n// backend/models/City.js\nconst mongoose = require('mongoose');\n\nconst citySchema = new mongoose.Schema(\n  {\n    name: {\n      type: String,\n      required: [true, 'Please provide a city name'],\n      trim: true,\n      index: true,\n    },\n    country: {\n      type: String,\n      required: [true, 'Please provide a country'],\n      trim: true,\n    },\n    countryCode: {\n      type: String,\n      required: true,\n      uppercase: true,\n      length: 2,\n    },\n    latitude: {\n      type: Number,\n      required: [true, 'Please provide latitude'],\n      min: -90,\n      max: 90,\n    },\n    longitude: {\n      type: Number,\n      required: [true, 'Please provide longitude'],\n      min: -180,\n      max: 180,\n    },\n    state: {\n      type: String,\n      trim: true,\n    },\n    population: {\n      type: Number,\n      default: null,\n    },\n    timezone: {\n      type: String,\n      default: 'UTC',\n    },\n    isCapital: {\n      type: Boolean,\n      default: false,\n    },\n    alternateNames: [String],\n    searchCount: {\n      type: Number,\n      default: 0,\n    },\n  },\n  {\n    timestamps: true,\n  }\n);\n\n// Create compound index for uniqueness\ncitySchema.index({ name: 1, countryCode: 1, latitude: 1, longitude: 1 }, { unique: true });\ncitySchema.index({ latitude: 1, longitude: 1 });\ncitySchema.index({ searchCount: -1 });\n\n// Instance methods\ncitySchema.methods.incrementSearchCount = async function () {\n  return this.updateOne({ $inc: { searchCount: 1 } });\n};\n\ncitySchema.methods.toJSON = function () {\n  return {\n    id: this._id,\n    name: this.name,\n    country: this.country,\n    countryCode: this.countryCode,\n    latitude: this.latitude,\n    longitude: this.longitude,\n    state: this.state,\n    population: this.population,\n    timezone: this.timezone,\n    isCapital: this.isCapital,\n  };\n};\n\n// Statics\ncitySchema.statics.findNearby = async function (latitude, longitude, maxDistance = 50000) {\n  return this.find({\n    location: {\n      $near: {\n        $geometry: {\n          type: 'Point',\n          coordinates: [longitude, latitude],\n        },\n        $maxDistance: maxDistance,\n      },\n    },\n  });\n};\n\nmodule.exports = mongoose.model('City', citySchema);\n```\n\n#### UserCity Model\n```javascript\n// backend/models/UserCity.js\nconst mongoose = require('mongoose');\n\nconst userCitySchema = new mongoose.Schema(\n  {\n    user: {\n      type: mongoose.Schema.Types.ObjectId,\n      ref: 'User',\n      required: true,\n    },\n    city: {\n      type: mongoose.Schema.Types.ObjectId,\n      ref: 'City',\n      required: true,\n    },\n    isDefault: {\n      type: Boolean,\n      default: false,\n    },\n    nickname: {\n      type: String,\n      trim: true,\n      maxlength: [50, 'Nickname must not exceed 50 characters'],\n    },\n    alerts: {\n      temperatureHigh: {\n        enabled: Boolean,\n        threshold: Number,\n      },\n      temperatureLow: {\n        enabled: Boolean,\n        threshold: Number,\n      },\n      precipitation: {\n        enabled: Boolean,\n        threshold: Number,\n      },\n      windSpeed: {\n        enabled: Boolean,\n        threshold: Number,\n      },\n    },\n    order: {\n      type: Number,\n      default: 0,\n    },\n  },\n  {\n    timestamps: true,\n  }\n);\n\n// Compound index for user and city\nuserCitySchema.index({ user: 1, city: 1 }, { unique: true });\nuserCitySchema.index({ user: 1, order: 1 });\n\n// Instance methods\nuserCitySchema.methods.setAsDefault = async function () {\n  await mongoose.model('UserCity').updateMany(\n    { user: this.user },\n    { isDefault: false }\n  );\n  this.isDefault = true;\n  return this.save();\n};\n\nuserCitySchema.methods.updateAlerts = async function (alertUpdates) {\n  Object.assign(this.alerts, alertUpdates);\n  return this.save();\n};\n\n// Statics\nuserCitySchema.statics.findUserCities = async function (userId) {\n  return this.find({ user: userId })\n    .populate('city')\n    .sort({ order: 1 });\n};\n\nuserCitySchema.statics.findDefaultCity = async function (userId) {\n  return this.findOne({ user: userId, isDefault: true }).populate('city');\n};\n\nmodule.exports = mongoose.model('UserCity', userCitySchema);\n```\n\n#### WeatherCache Model\n```javascript\n// backend/models/WeatherCache.js\nconst mongoose = require('mongoose');\n\nconst weatherCacheSchema = new mongoose.Schema(\n  {\n    city: {\n      type: mongoose.Schema.Types.ObjectId,\n      ref: 'City',\n      required: true,\n    },\n    cacheType: {\n      type: String,\n      enum: ['current', 'forecast', 'hourly'],\n      required: true,\n    },\n    data: {\n      type: mongoose.Schema.Types.Mixed,\n      required: true,\n    },\n    source: {\n      type: String,\n      enum: ['openweathermap', 'weatherapi', 'weatherstack'],\n      default: 'openweathermap',\n    },\n    expiresAt: {\n      type: Date,\n      required: true,\n      index: { expireAfterSeconds: 0 },\n    },\n    hitCount: {\n      type: Number,\n      default: 0,\n    },\n  },\n  {\n    timestamps: true,\n  }\n);\n\n// Compound index\nweatherCacheSchema.index({ city: 1, cacheType: 1 }, { unique: true });\n\n// Instance methods\nweatherCacheSchema.methods.isExpired = function () {\n  return this.expiresAt < new Date();\n};\n\nweatherCacheSchema.methods.incrementHitCount = async function () {\n  return this.updateOne({ $inc: { hitCount: 1 } });\n};\n\nweatherCacheSchema.methods.refresh = async function (newData, ttlSeconds = 600) {\n  this.data = newData;\n  this.expiresAt = new Date(Date.now() + ttlSeconds * 1000);\n  this.hitCount = 0;\n  return this.save();\n};\n\n// Statics\nweatherCacheSchema.statics.findOrCreateCache = async function (cityId, cacheType, ttlSeconds = 600) {\n  let cache = await this.findOne({ city: cityId, cacheType });\n\n  if (!cache) {\n    cache = await this.create({\n      city: cityId,\n      cacheType,\n      data: {},\n      expiresAt: new Date(Date.now() + ttlSeconds * 1000),\n    });\n  }\n\n  return cache;\n};\n\nweatherCacheSchema.statics.clearExpired = async function () {\n  return this.deleteMany({ expiresAt: { $lt: new Date() } });\n};\n\nmodule.exports = mongoose.model('WeatherCache', weatherCacheSchema);\n```\n\n#### APILog Model\n```javascript\n// backend/models/APILog.js\nconst mongoose = require('mongoose');\n\nconst apiLogSchema = new mongoose.Schema(\n  {\n    user: {\n      type: mongoose.Schema.Types.ObjectId,\n      ref: 'User',\n      default: null,\n    },\n    endpoint: {\n      type: String,\n      required: true,\n      index: true,\n    },\n    method: {\n      type: String,\n      enum: ['GET', 'POST', 'PUT', 'DELETE', 'PATCH'],\n      required: true,\n    },\n    statusCode: {\n      type: Number,\n      required: true,\n      index: true,\n    },\n    responseTime: {\n      type: Number,\n      required: true,\n    },\n    requestSize: Number,\n    responseSize: Number,\n    errorMessage: String,\n    ipAddress: String,\n    userAgent: String,\n    externalAPICall: {\n      provider: String,\n      endpoint: String,\n      statusCode: Number,\n      responseTime: Number,\n    },\n    metadata: mongoose.Schema.Types.Mixed,\n  },\n  {\n    timestamps: true,\n  }\n);\n\n// Indexes for efficient querying\napiLogSchema.index({ createdAt: -1 });\napiLogSchema.index({ user: 1, createdAt: -1 });\napiLogSchema.index({ endpoint: 1, createdAt: -1 });\napiLogSchema.index({ statusCode: 1, createdAt: -1 });\n\n// TTL index for automatic deletion after 30 days\napiLog", "tool_call_id": "tooluse_nj85BN6QhdWmE7IyacaVSn", "name": "delegate_work_to_coworker"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "", "tool_calls": [{"id": "tooluse_PC0WnGopOkBCTyB8MS9Iv9", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "ask_question_to_coworker", "arguments": "{\"context\": \"We're receiving a comprehensive code outline. So far we have received:\\n- Middleware layer (auth, error handling, rate limiting, logging)\\n- Models (User, City, UserCity, WeatherCache, APILog)\\n\\nWe still need the COMPLETE actual code for:\\n1. Services Layer (AuthService, WeatherService, UserService, CityService, CacheService, ExternalWeatherAPI)\\n2. Controllers Layer (AuthController, WeatherController, UserController, CityController)\\n3. Routes Layer (authRoutes, weatherRoutes, userRoutes, cityRoutes)\\n4. Utils (validators, errorFormatter, tokenGenerator, weatherDataMapper)\\n5. Main app.js and server.js files\\n\\nFRONTEND:\\n1. Redux store setup and slices (authSlice, weatherSlice, userSlice, citySlice, uiSlice, settingsSlice)\\n2. Thunks for async operations\\n3. Selectors\\n4. API client with interceptors\\n5. Services (AuthService, WeatherService, UserService, CityService)\\n6. Custom hooks (useAuth, useWeather, useCity, useSettings, useFetch)\\n7. React components (Auth, Dashboard, Weather, Search, Settings, Common)\\n8. Pages (LoginPage, RegisterPage, DashboardPage, WeatherDetailPage, SettingsPage)\\n9. App.jsx and routing setup\\n\\nProvide the COMPLETE, ACTUAL code for all of these - not summaries, the full implementations.\", \"coworker\": \"Coding Specialist\", \"question\": \"Please provide the COMPLETE actual code for all remaining components: Services (Auth, Weather, User, City, Cache, ExternalWeatherAPI), Controllers (Auth, Weather, User, City), Routes, Utils, app.js/server.js, AND the complete Frontend including Redux slices/thunks/selectors, API client, services, custom hooks, all React components, pages, App.jsx, and routing. This must be the actual full code content for every file, not summaries or abbreviated versions.\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "content": "I'll provide the complete, actual code for all remaining components. This is a comprehensive weather application with authentication, caching, and external API integration.\n\n## BACKEND\n\n### 1. Services Layer\n\n#### services/AuthService.js\n```javascript\nconst jwt = require('jsonwebtoken');\nconst bcrypt = require('bcryptjs');\nconst User = require('../models/User');\nconst { AppError } = require('../utils/errorFormatter');\n\nclass AuthService {\n  async register(userData) {\n    const { email, password, firstName, lastName } = userData;\n\n    // Check if user already exists\n    const existingUser = await User.findOne({ email });\n    if (existingUser) {\n      throw new AppError('Email already registered', 400);\n    }\n\n    // Hash password\n    const salt = await bcrypt.genSalt(10);\n    const hashedPassword = await bcrypt.hash(password, salt);\n\n    // Create user\n    const user = await User.create({\n      email,\n      password: hashedPassword,\n      firstName,\n      lastName,\n      isEmailVerified: false,\n    });\n\n    // Generate tokens\n    const tokens = this.generateTokens(user._id, user.email);\n\n    return {\n      user: {\n        id: user._id,\n        email: user.email,\n        firstName: user.firstName,\n        lastName: user.lastName,\n      },\n      tokens,\n    };\n  }\n\n  async login(email, password) {\n    // Find user\n    const user = await User.findOne({ email });\n    if (!user) {\n      throw new AppError('Invalid email or password', 401);\n    }\n\n    // Compare passwords\n    const isPasswordValid = await bcrypt.compare(password, user.password);\n    if (!isPasswordValid) {\n      throw new AppError('Invalid email or password', 401);\n    }\n\n    // Update last login\n    user.lastLogin = new Date();\n    await user.save();\n\n    // Generate tokens\n    const tokens = this.generateTokens(user._id, user.email);\n\n    return {\n      user: {\n        id: user._id,\n        email: user.email,\n        firstName: user.firstName,\n        lastName: user.lastName,\n      },\n      tokens,\n    };\n  }\n\n  async refreshToken(refreshToken) {\n    try {\n      const decoded = jwt.verify(\n        refreshToken,\n        process.env.JWT_REFRESH_SECRET || 'refresh_secret_key'\n      );\n\n      const user = await User.findById(decoded.userId);\n      if (!user) {\n        throw new AppError('User not found', 404);\n      }\n\n      const tokens = this.generateTokens(user._id, user.email);\n\n      return tokens;\n    } catch (error) {\n      throw new AppError('Invalid refresh token', 401);\n    }\n  }\n\n  async verifyToken(token) {\n    try {\n      const decoded = jwt.verify(\n        token,\n        process.env.JWT_SECRET || 'secret_key'\n      );\n      return decoded;\n    } catch (error) {\n      throw new AppError('Invalid token', 401);\n    }\n  }\n\n  generateTokens(userId, email) {\n    const accessToken = jwt.sign(\n      { userId, email },\n      process.env.JWT_SECRET || 'secret_key',\n      { expiresIn: '15m' }\n    );\n\n    const refreshToken = jwt.sign(\n      { userId, email },\n      process.env.JWT_REFRESH_SECRET || 'refresh_secret_key',\n      { expiresIn: '7d' }\n    );\n\n    return { accessToken, refreshToken };\n  }\n\n  async logout(userId) {\n    // Optional: Invalidate tokens in blacklist or database\n    // For now, client-side logout is sufficient\n    return { message: 'Logged out successfully' };\n  }\n\n  async changePassword(userId, oldPassword, newPassword) {\n    const user = await User.findById(userId);\n    if (!user) {\n      throw new AppError('User not found', 404);\n    }\n\n    const isPasswordValid = await bcrypt.compare(oldPassword, user.password);\n    if (!isPasswordValid) {\n      throw new AppError('Current password is incorrect', 401);\n    }\n\n    const salt = await bcrypt.genSalt(10);\n    user.password = await bcrypt.hash(newPassword, salt);\n    await user.save();\n\n    return { message: 'Password changed successfully' };\n  }\n\n  async resetPassword(email) {\n    const user = await User.findOne({ email });\n    if (!user) {\n      throw new AppError('User not found', 404);\n    }\n\n    // Generate reset token (valid for 1 hour)\n    const resetToken = jwt.sign(\n      { userId: user._id, type: 'reset' },\n      process.env.JWT_SECRET || 'secret_key',\n      { expiresIn: '1h' }\n    );\n\n    return { resetToken, email: user.email };\n  }\n}\n\nmodule.exports = new AuthService();\n```\n\n#### services/WeatherService.js\n```javascript\nconst WeatherCache = require('../models/WeatherCache');\nconst ExternalWeatherAPI = require('./ExternalWeatherAPI');\nconst { weatherDataMapper } = require('../utils/weatherDataMapper');\nconst { AppError } = require('../utils/errorFormatter');\n\nclass WeatherService {\n  async getWeatherByCityId(cityId, options = {}) {\n    const { forceRefresh = false } = options;\n\n    if (!forceRefresh) {\n      // Try to get from cache\n      const cachedData = await this.getCachedWeather(cityId);\n      if (cachedData) {\n        return cachedData;\n      }\n    }\n\n    // Fetch from external API\n    const city = await require('../models/City').findById(cityId);\n    if (!city) {\n      throw new AppError('City not found', 404);\n    }\n\n    const weatherData = await ExternalWeatherAPI.getWeatherByCoordinates(\n      city.latitude,\n      city.longitude\n    );\n\n    // Map and cache the data\n    const mappedData = weatherDataMapper(weatherData, city);\n\n    await this.cacheWeather(cityId, mappedData);\n\n    return mappedData;\n  }\n\n  async getWeatherByCoordinates(latitude, longitude, options = {}) {\n    const { forceRefresh = false } = options;\n\n    // Fetch from external API\n    const weatherData = await ExternalWeatherAPI.getWeatherByCoordinates(\n      latitude,\n      longitude\n    );\n\n    return weatherDataMapper(weatherData, { latitude, longitude });\n  }\n\n  async getCachedWeather(cityId) {\n    const cache = await WeatherCache.findOne({ city: cityId });\n\n    if (!cache) {\n      return null;\n    }\n\n    // Check if cache is still valid (less than 30 minutes old)\n    const cacheAge = Date.now() - cache.createdAt.getTime();\n    const thirtyMinutes = 30 * 60 * 1000;\n\n    if (cacheAge > thirtyMinutes) {\n      await WeatherCache.deleteOne({ _id: cache._id });\n      return null;\n    }\n\n    return cache.data;\n  }\n\n  async cacheWeather(cityId, weatherData) {\n    await WeatherCache.findOneAndUpdate(\n      { city: cityId },\n      { data: weatherData, city: cityId },\n      { upsert: true, new: true }\n    );\n  }\n\n  async getWeatherForecast(cityId, days = 5, options = {}) {\n    const { forceRefresh = false } = options;\n\n    const city = await require('../models/City').findById(cityId);\n    if (!city) {\n      throw new AppError('City not found', 404);\n    }\n\n    const forecastData = await ExternalWeatherAPI.getWeatherForecast(\n      city.latitude,\n      city.longitude,\n      days\n    );\n\n    return {\n      city: {\n        id: city._id,\n        name: city.name,\n        country: city.country,\n      },\n      forecast: forecastData,\n    };\n  }\n\n  async getMultipleCitiesWeather(cityIds) {\n    const weatherDataArray = await Promise.all(\n      cityIds.map(cityId => this.getWeatherByCityId(cityId))\n    );\n\n    return weatherDataArray;\n  }\n\n  async clearCache(cityId) {\n    await WeatherCache.deleteOne({ city: cityId });\n    return { message: 'Cache cleared successfully' };\n  }\n\n  async clearAllCache() {\n    await WeatherCache.deleteMany({});\n    return { message: 'All cache cleared successfully' };\n  }\n\n  async getWeatherAlerts(cityId) {\n    const city = await require('../models/City').findById(cityId);\n    if (!city) {\n      throw new AppError('City not found', 404);\n    }\n\n    const alerts = await ExternalWeatherAPI.getWeatherAlerts(\n      city.latitude,\n      city.longitude\n    );\n\n    return alerts;\n  }\n}\n\nmodule.exports = new WeatherService();\n```\n\n#### services/UserService.js\n```javascript\nconst User = require('../models/User');\nconst UserCity = require('../models/UserCity');\nconst { AppError } = require('../utils/errorFormatter');\n\nclass UserService {\n  async getUserById(userId) {\n    const user = await User.findById(userId).select('-password');\n    if (!user) {\n      throw new AppError('User not found', 404);\n    }\n    return user;\n  }\n\n  async getUserProfile(userId) {\n    const user = await User.findById(userId)\n      .select('-password')\n      .populate('favoriteCities');\n\n    if (!user) {\n      throw new AppError('User not found', 404);\n    }\n\n    const userCities = await UserCity.find({ user: userId }).populate('city');\n\n    return {\n      ...user.toObject(),\n      cities: userCities,\n    };\n  }\n\n  async updateUserProfile(userId, updateData) {\n    const allowedFields = ['firstName', 'lastName', 'preferences', 'theme'];\n    const updateObj = {};\n\n    allowedFields.forEach(field => {\n      if (updateData[field] !== undefined) {\n        updateObj[field] = updateData[field];\n      }\n    });\n\n    const user = await User.findByIdAndUpdate(userId, updateObj, {\n      new: true,\n      runValidators: true,\n    }).select('-password');\n\n    if (!user) {\n      throw new AppError('User not found', 404);\n    }\n\n    return user;\n  }\n\n  async addFavoriteCity(userId, cityId) {\n    const user = await User.findById(userId);\n    if (!user) {\n      throw new AppError('User not found', 404);\n    }\n\n    const city = await require('../models/City').findById(cityId);\n    if (!city) {\n      throw new AppError('City not found', 404);\n    }\n\n    // Check if already exists\n    const existingUserCity = await UserCity.findOne({\n      user: userId,\n      city: cityId,\n    });\n\n    if (existingUserCity) {\n      throw new AppError('City already added to favorites', 400);\n    }\n\n    const userCity = await UserCity.create({\n      user: userId,\n      city: cityId,\n      isFavorite: true,\n    });\n\n    if (!user.favoriteCities.includes(cityId)) {\n      user.favoriteCities.push(cityId);\n      await user.save();\n    }\n\n    return userCity.populate('city');\n  }\n\n  async removeFavoriteCity(userId, cityId) {\n    const userCity = await UserCity.findOneAndDelete({\n      user: userId,\n      city: cityId,\n    });\n\n    if (!userCity) {\n      throw new AppError('City not found in favorites', 404);\n    }\n\n    await User.findByIdAndUpdate(userId, {\n      $pull: { favoriteCities: cityId },\n    });\n\n    return { message: 'City removed from favorites' };\n  }\n\n  async getFavoriteCities(userId) {\n    const userCities = await UserCity.find({ user: userId, isFavorite: true })\n      .populate('city')\n      .sort({ createdAt: -1 });\n\n    return userCities;\n  }\n\n  async updateUserPreferences(userId, preferences) {\n    const user = await User.findByIdAndUpdate(\n      userId,\n      { preferences },\n      { new: true, runValidators: true }\n    ).select('-password');\n\n    if (!user) {\n      throw new AppError('User not found', 404);\n    }\n\n    return user;\n  }\n\n  async deleteUserAccount(userId) {\n    const user = await User.findById(userId);\n    if (!user) {\n      throw new AppError('User not found', 404);\n    }\n\n    // Delete related data\n    await UserCity.deleteMany({ user: userId });\n\n    // Delete user\n    await User.findByIdAndDelete(userId);\n\n    return { message: 'User account deleted successfully' };\n  }\n\n  async searchUsers(query) {\n    const users = await User.find({\n      $or: [\n        { email: { $regex: query, $options: 'i' } },\n        { firstName: { $regex: query, $options: 'i' } },\n        { lastName: { $regex: query, $options: 'i' } },\n      ],\n    })\n      .select('-password')\n      .limit(10);\n\n    return users;\n  }\n}\n\nmodule.exports = new UserService();\n```\n\n#### services/CityService.js\n```javascript\nconst City = require('../models/City');\nconst { AppError } = require('../utils/errorFormatter');\n\nclass CityService {\n  async getAllCities(filters = {}) {\n    const { page = 1, limit = 20, search, country } = filters;\n    const skip = (page - 1) * limit;\n\n    let query = {};\n\n    if (search) {\n      query.$or = [\n        { name: { $regex: search, $options: 'i' } },\n        { country: { $regex: search, $options: 'i' } },\n      ];\n    }\n\n    if (country) {\n      query.country = country;\n    }\n\n    const total = await City.countDocuments(query);\n    const cities = await City.find(query)\n      .skip(skip)\n      .limit(limit)\n      .sort({ name: 1 });\n\n    return {\n      cities,\n      pagination: {\n        total,\n        page,\n        limit,\n        pages: Math.ceil(total / limit),\n      },\n    };\n  }\n\n  async getCityById(cityId) {\n    const city = await City.findById(cityId);\n    if (!city) {\n      throw new AppError('City not found', 404);\n    }\n    return city;\n  }\n\n  async searchCities(query) {\n    const cities = await City.find({\n      $or: [\n        { name: { $regex: query, $options: 'i' } },\n        { country: { $regex: query, $options: 'i' } },\n      ],\n    })\n      .limit(20)\n      .sort({ name: 1 });\n\n    return cities;\n  }\n\n  async getCitiesByCountry(country) {\n    const cities = await City.find({ country }).sort({ name: 1 });\n    return cities;\n  }\n\n  async createCity(cityData) {\n    const { name, country, latitude, longitude } = cityData;\n\n    // Check if city already exists\n    const existingCity = await City.findOne({ name, country });\n    if (existingCity) {\n      throw new AppError('City already exists', 400);\n    }\n\n    const city = await City.create({\n      name,\n      country,\n      latitude,\n      longitude,\n    });\n\n    return city;\n  }\n\n  async updateCity(cityId, updateData) {\n    const city = await City.findByIdAndUpdate(cityId, updateData, {\n      new: true,\n      runValidators: true,\n    });\n\n    if (!city) {\n      throw new AppError('City not found', 404);\n    }\n\n    return city;\n  }\n\n  async deleteCity(cityId) {\n    const city = await City.findByIdAndDelete(", "tool_call_id": "tooluse_PC0WnGopOkBCTyB8MS9Iv9", "name": "ask_question_to_coworker"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "", "tool_calls": [{"id": "tooluse_kOLGX3TbcFgw6g1f0nMss0", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "delegate_work_to_coworker", "arguments": "{\"context\": \"We need the COMPLETE, FINAL code outline that includes everything we haven't received yet. We have received partial Services code. We still need:\\n\\nBACKEND (Complete):\\n1. Complete CityService (deleteCity and remaining methods)\\n2. CacheService (full implementation)\\n3. ExternalWeatherAPI (full implementation with OpenWeatherMap, WeatherAPI, NOAA integration)\\n4. Controllers (AuthController, WeatherController, UserController, CityController with all methods)\\n5. Routes (authRoutes, weatherRoutes, userRoutes, cityRoutes with all endpoints and middleware)\\n6. Utils (validators.js, errorFormatter.js, tokenGenerator.js, weatherDataMapper.js)\\n7. app.js (Express app setup with all middleware)\\n8. server.js (Server startup)\\n\\nFRONTEND (Complete):\\n1. Redux store configuration (store/index.js)\\n2. Redux slices (authSlice, weatherSlice, userSlice, citySlice, uiSlice, settingsSlice)\\n3. Redux thunks (authThunks, weatherThunks, userThunks, cityThunks)\\n4. Redux selectors (authSelectors, weatherSelectors, citySelectors, settingsSelectors)\\n5. API client (axiosInstance.js, apiClient.js, endpoints.js, interceptors.js)\\n6. Services (AuthService, WeatherService, UserService, CityService)\\n7. Custom hooks (useAuth, useWeather, useCity, useSettings, useFetch, useLocalStorage)\\n8. All React Components (Auth, Dashboard, Weather, Search, Settings, Common, Layout)\\n9. All Pages (LoginPage, RegisterPage, DashboardPage, WeatherDetailPage, SettingsPage)\\n10. App.jsx with routing\\n11. index.jsx (entry point)\\n\\nReturn the COMPLETE actual code for all of these files, not summaries. This is the final answer that should contain everything.\", \"coworker\": \"Coding Specialist\", \"task\": \"Provide the COMPLETE, FULL, ACTUAL code outline for the weather app. This is the final comprehensive output that must include: Complete CityService, CacheService, ExternalWeatherAPI, all Controllers, all Routes with middleware, all Utils, app.js, server.js, complete Redux setup (store, slices, thunks, selectors), API client with interceptors, all Services, all custom hooks, all React components, all pages, App.jsx, and index.jsx. This must be the actual complete code for every single file, not abbreviated or summarized.\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "content": "I'll provide the complete, comprehensive code outline for the entire weather app. This is the actual, full implementation for every single file.\n\n## BACKEND CODE\n\n### server.js\n```javascript\nconst app = require('./app');\nconst dotenv = require('dotenv');\n\ndotenv.config();\n\nconst PORT = process.env.PORT || 5000;\nconst NODE_ENV = process.env.NODE_ENV || 'development';\n\nconst server = app.listen(PORT, () => {\n  console.log(`🚀 Server running in ${NODE_ENV} mode on port ${PORT}`);\n  console.log(`📍 API Base URL: http://localhost:${PORT}`);\n});\n\nprocess.on('unhandledRejection', (err) => {\n  console.error('❌ Unhandled Rejection:', err);\n  server.close(() => process.exit(1));\n});\n\nprocess.on('SIGTERM', () => {\n  console.log('⚠️  SIGTERM received, shutting down gracefully');\n  server.close(() => {\n    console.log('✅ Process terminated');\n    process.exit(0);\n  });\n});\n\nmodule.exports = server;\n```\n\n### app.js\n```javascript\nconst express = require('express');\nconst cors = require('cors');\nconst helmet = require('helmet');\nconst mongoSanitize = require('express-mongo-sanitize');\nconst rateLimit = require('express-rate-limit');\nconst morgan = require('morgan');\nconst dotenv = require('dotenv');\n\n// Import routes\nconst authRoutes = require('./routes/authRoutes');\nconst weatherRoutes = require('./routes/weatherRoutes');\nconst userRoutes = require('./routes/userRoutes');\nconst cityRoutes = require('./routes/cityRoutes');\n\n// Import middleware\nconst errorHandler = require('./middleware/errorHandler');\nconst authenticate = require('./middleware/authenticate');\n\ndotenv.config();\n\nconst app = express();\n\n// Security Middleware\napp.use(helmet());\napp.use(mongoSanitize());\n\n// CORS Configuration\nconst corsOptions = {\n  origin: process.env.CORS_ORIGIN || 'http://localhost:3000',\n  credentials: true,\n  optionsSuccessStatus: 200,\n  methods: ['GET', 'POST', 'PUT', 'DELETE', 'PATCH', 'OPTIONS'],\n  allowedHeaders: ['Content-Type', 'Authorization']\n};\napp.use(cors(corsOptions));\n\n// Rate Limiting\nconst limiter = rateLimit({\n  windowMs: 15 * 60 * 1000,\n  max: 100,\n  message: 'Too many requests from this IP, please try again later.'\n});\napp.use(limiter);\n\n// Logging\nif (process.env.NODE_ENV === 'development') {\n  app.use(morgan('dev'));\n} else {\n  app.use(morgan('combined'));\n}\n\n// Body Parser Middleware\napp.use(express.json({ limit: '10kb' }));\napp.use(express.urlencoded({ limit: '10kb', extended: true }));\n\n// Health Check Route\napp.get('/api/health', (req, res) => {\n  res.status(200).json({\n    status: 'success',\n    message: 'Server is running',\n    timestamp: new Date().toISOString()\n  });\n});\n\n// API Routes\napp.use('/api/auth', authRoutes);\napp.use('/api/weather', weatherRoutes);\napp.use('/api/users', authenticate, userRoutes);\napp.use('/api/cities', authenticate, cityRoutes);\n\n// 404 Handler\napp.use('*', (req, res) => {\n  res.status(404).json({\n    status: 'error',\n    message: `Route ${req.originalUrl} not found`\n  });\n});\n\n// Global Error Handler\napp.use(errorHandler);\n\nmodule.exports = app;\n```\n\n### middleware/authenticate.js\n```javascript\nconst jwt = require('jsonwebtoken');\nconst User = require('../models/User');\n\nconst authenticate = async (req, res, next) => {\n  try {\n    const token = req.headers.authorization?.split(' ')[1];\n\n    if (!token) {\n      return res.status(401).json({\n        status: 'error',\n        message: 'No token provided'\n      });\n    }\n\n    const decoded = jwt.verify(token, process.env.JWT_SECRET);\n    const user = await User.findById(decoded.id);\n\n    if (!user) {\n      return res.status(401).json({\n        status: 'error',\n        message: 'User not found'\n      });\n    }\n\n    req.user = user;\n    next();\n  } catch (error) {\n    if (error.name === 'TokenExpiredError') {\n      return res.status(401).json({\n        status: 'error',\n        message: 'Token expired'\n      });\n    }\n    res.status(401).json({\n      status: 'error',\n      message: 'Invalid token'\n    });\n  }\n};\n\nmodule.exports = authenticate;\n```\n\n### middleware/errorHandler.js\n```javascript\nconst errorHandler = (err, req, res, next) => {\n  console.error('Error:', err);\n\n  const statusCode = err.statusCode || 500;\n  const message = err.message || 'Internal Server Error';\n\n  res.status(statusCode).json({\n    status: 'error',\n    message,\n    ...(process.env.NODE_ENV === 'development' && { stack: err.stack })\n  });\n};\n\nmodule.exports = errorHandler;\n```\n\n### models/User.js\n```javascript\nconst mongoose = require('mongoose');\nconst bcrypt = require('bcryptjs');\n\nconst userSchema = new mongoose.Schema(\n  {\n    name: {\n      type: String,\n      required: [true, 'Please provide a name'],\n      trim: true\n    },\n    email: {\n      type: String,\n      required: [true, 'Please provide an email'],\n      unique: true,\n      lowercase: true,\n      match: [/^\\w+([.-]?\\w+)*@\\w+([.-]?\\w+)*(\\.\\w{2,3})+$/, 'Please provide a valid email']\n    },\n    password: {\n      type: String,\n      required: [true, 'Please provide a password'],\n      minlength: 6,\n      select: false\n    },\n    temperatureUnit: {\n      type: String,\n      enum: ['C', 'F', 'K'],\n      default: 'C'\n    },\n    windSpeedUnit: {\n      type: String,\n      enum: ['ms', 'kmh', 'mph'],\n      default: 'ms'\n    },\n    pressureUnit: {\n      type: String,\n      enum: ['hPa', 'mmHg', 'inHg'],\n      default: 'hPa'\n    },\n    theme: {\n      type: String,\n      enum: ['light', 'dark'],\n      default: 'light'\n    },\n    notifications: {\n      enabled: {\n        type: Boolean,\n        default: true\n      },\n      frequency: {\n        type: String,\n        enum: ['realtime', 'hourly', 'daily'],\n        default: 'daily'\n      }\n    },\n    createdAt: {\n      type: Date,\n      default: Date.now\n    },\n    updatedAt: {\n      type: Date,\n      default: Date.now\n    }\n  },\n  { timestamps: true }\n);\n\nuserSchema.pre('save', async function (next) {\n  if (!this.isModified('password')) return next();\n\n  try {\n    const salt = await bcrypt.genSalt(10);\n    this.password = await bcrypt.hash(this.password, salt);\n    next();\n  } catch (error) {\n    next(error);\n  }\n});\n\nuserSchema.methods.comparePassword = async function (enteredPassword) {\n  return await bcrypt.compare(enteredPassword, this.password);\n};\n\nmodule.exports = mongoose.model('User', userSchema);\n```\n\n### models/City.js\n```javascript\nconst mongoose = require('mongoose');\n\nconst citySchema = new mongoose.Schema(\n  {\n    userId: {\n      type: mongoose.Schema.Types.ObjectId,\n      ref: 'User',\n      required: true\n    },\n    name: {\n      type: String,\n      required: [true, 'City name is required'],\n      trim: true\n    },\n    latitude: {\n      type: Number,\n      required: true\n    },\n    longitude: {\n      type: Number,\n      required: true\n    },\n    country: {\n      type: String,\n      required: true\n    },\n    state: String,\n    isFavorite: {\n      type: Boolean,\n      default: false\n    },\n    isDefault: {\n      type: Boolean,\n      default: false\n    },\n    lastUpdated: {\n      type: Date,\n      default: Date.now\n    },\n    createdAt: {\n      type: Date,\n      default: Date.now\n    },\n    updatedAt: {\n      type: Date,\n      default: Date.now\n    }\n  },\n  { timestamps: true }\n);\n\ncitySchema.index({ userId: 1, name: 1 });\ncitySchema.index({ userId: 1, isFavorite: 1 });\n\nmodule.exports = mongoose.model('City', citySchema);\n```\n\n### utils/validators.js\n```javascript\nconst validateEmail = (email) => {\n  const emailRegex = /^\\w+([.-]?\\w+)*@\\w+([.-]?\\w+)*(\\.\\w{2,3})+$/;\n  return emailRegex.test(email);\n};\n\nconst validatePassword = (password) => {\n  if (password.length < 6) {\n    return {\n      valid: false,\n      message: 'Password must be at least 6 characters long'\n    };\n  }\n  return { valid: true };\n};\n\nconst validateCoordinates = (latitude, longitude) => {\n  const lat = parseFloat(latitude);\n  const lon = parseFloat(longitude);\n\n  if (isNaN(lat) || isNaN(lon)) {\n    return {\n      valid: false,\n      message: 'Invalid coordinates format'\n    };\n  }\n\n  if (lat < -90 || lat > 90) {\n    return {\n      valid: false,\n      message: 'Latitude must be between -90 and 90'\n    };\n  }\n\n  if (lon < -180 || lon > 180) {\n    return {\n      valid: false,\n      message: 'Longitude must be between -180 and 180'\n    };\n  }\n\n  return { valid: true };\n};\n\nconst validateTemperatureUnit = (unit) => {\n  const validUnits = ['C', 'F', 'K'];\n  return validUnits.includes(unit);\n};\n\nconst validateWindSpeedUnit = (unit) => {\n  const validUnits = ['ms', 'kmh', 'mph'];\n  return validUnits.includes(unit);\n};\n\nconst validatePressureUnit = (unit) => {\n  const validUnits = ['hPa', 'mmHg', 'inHg'];\n  return validUnits.includes(unit);\n};\n\nmodule.exports = {\n  validateEmail,\n  validatePassword,\n  validateCoordinates,\n  validateTemperatureUnit,\n  validateWindSpeedUnit,\n  validatePressureUnit\n};\n```\n\n### utils/errorFormatter.js\n```javascript\nclass AppError extends Error {\n  constructor(message, statusCode) {\n    super(message);\n    this.statusCode = statusCode;\n    Error.captureStackTrace(this, this.constructor);\n  }\n}\n\nconst formatError = (error) => {\n  if (error instanceof AppError) {\n    return {\n      status: 'error',\n      message: error.message,\n      statusCode: error.statusCode\n    };\n  }\n\n  if (error.name === 'ValidationError') {\n    const messages = Object.values(error.errors).map(err => err.message);\n    return {\n      status: 'error',\n      message: 'Validation Error',\n      details: messages,\n      statusCode: 400\n    };\n  }\n\n  if (error.name === 'CastError') {\n    return {\n      status: 'error',\n      message: 'Invalid ID format',\n      statusCode: 400\n    };\n  }\n\n  return {\n    status: 'error',\n    message: error.message || 'Internal Server Error',\n    statusCode: 500\n  };\n};\n\nmodule.exports = {\n  AppError,\n  formatError\n};\n```\n\n### utils/tokenGenerator.js\n```javascript\nconst jwt = require('jsonwebtoken');\n\nconst generateToken = (userId) => {\n  const token = jwt.sign(\n    { id: userId },\n    process.env.JWT_SECRET,\n    {\n      expiresIn: process.env.JWT_EXPIRE || '7d'\n    }\n  );\n  return token;\n};\n\nconst verifyToken = (token) => {\n  try {\n    const decoded = jwt.verify(token, process.env.JWT_SECRET);\n    return { valid: true, decoded };\n  } catch (error) {\n    return { valid: false, error: error.message };\n  }\n};\n\nmodule.exports = {\n  generateToken,\n  verifyToken\n};\n```\n\n### utils/weatherDataMapper.js\n```javascript\nconst convertTemperature = (temp, fromUnit, toUnit) => {\n  let celsius = temp;\n\n  if (fromUnit === 'F') {\n    celsius = (temp - 32) * (5 / 9);\n  } else if (fromUnit === 'K') {\n    celsius = temp - 273.15;\n  }\n\n  if (toUnit === 'F') {\n    return celsius * (9 / 5) + 32;\n  } else if (toUnit === 'K') {\n    return celsius + 273.15;\n  }\n\n  return celsius;\n};\n\nconst convertWindSpeed = (speed, fromUnit, toUnit) => {\n  let ms = speed;\n\n  if (fromUnit === 'kmh') {\n    ms = speed / 3.6;\n  } else if (fromUnit === 'mph') {\n    ms = speed / 2.237;\n  }\n\n  if (toUnit === 'kmh') {\n    return ms * 3.6;\n  } else if (toUnit === 'mph') {\n    return ms * 2.237;\n  }\n\n  return ms;\n};\n\nconst convertPressure = (pressure, fromUnit, toUnit) => {\n  let hpa = pressure;\n\n  if (fromUnit === 'mmHg') {\n    hpa = pressure / 0.75006;\n  } else if (fromUnit === 'inHg') {\n    hpa = pressure * 33.8639;\n  }\n\n  if (toUnit === 'mmHg') {\n    return hpa * 0.75006;\n  } else if (toUnit === 'inHg') {\n    return hpa / 33.8639;\n  }\n\n  return hpa;\n};\n\nconst mapOpenWeatherMapData = (data) => {\n  return {\n    city: data.name,\n    country: data.sys.country,\n    latitude: data.coord.lat,\n    longitude: data.coord.lon,\n    temperature: data.main.temp,\n    feelsLike: data.main.feels_like,\n    humidity: data.main.humidity,\n    pressure: data.main.pressure,\n    windSpeed: data.wind.speed,\n    windDirection: data.wind.deg,\n    cloudiness: data.clouds.all,\n    visibility: data.visibility,\n    precipitation: data.rain?.['1h'] || 0,\n    description: data.weather[0].description,\n    icon: data.weather[0].icon,\n    sunrise: new Date(data.sys.sunrise * 1000),\n    sunset: new Date(data.sys.sunset * 1000),\n    timestamp: new Date(data.dt * 1000)\n  };\n};\n\nconst mapWeatherAPIData = (data) => {\n  const current = data.current;\n  return {\n    city: data.location.name,\n    country: data.location.country,\n    latitude: data.location.lat,\n    longitude: data.location.lon,\n    temperature: current.temp_c", "tool_call_id": "tooluse_kOLGX3TbcFgw6g1f0nMss0", "name": "delegate_work_to_coworker"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Perfect! I've received substantial portions of the code. Let me now compile the final comprehensive answer with all the remaining components to provide you with the complete code outline.\n\n## **COMPLETE WEATHER APP CODE OUTLINE**\n\nBased on the comprehensive research and detailed project plan, here is the **complete code structure for the weather app**:\n\n---\n\n# **WEATHER APP - COMPLETE CODE STRUCTURE & ARCHITECTURE**\n\n## **DIRECTORY STRUCTURE**\n\n```\nweather-app/\n├── backend/\n│   ├── src/\n│   │   ├── config/\n│   │   │   ├── database.js          # Database connection & pooling\n│   │   │   ├── cache.js             # Redis cache configuration\n│   │   │   └── environment.js       # Environment variables\n│   │   ├── middleware/\n│   │   │   ├── authenticate.js      # JWT authentication\n│   │   │   ├── errorHandler.js      # Global error handling\n│   │   │   ├── rateLimiter.js       # Rate limiting\n│   │   │   └── logging.js           # Request logging\n│   │   ├── models/\n│   │   │   ├── User.js              # User schema & methods\n│   │   │   ├── City.js              # City schema & methods\n│   │   │   ├── UserCity.js          # User-City relationship\n│   │   │   ├── WeatherCache.js      # Weather data cache\n│   │   │   └── APILog.js            # API call logging\n│   │   ├── services/\n│   │   │   ├── AuthService.js       # Authentication logic\n│   │   │   ├── WeatherService.js    # Weather data operations\n│   │   │   ├── UserService.js       # User management\n│   │   │   ├── CityService.js       # City operations\n│   │   │   ├── CacheService.js      # Cache management\n│   │   │   └── ExternalWeatherAPI.js # External API integration\n│   │   ├── controllers/\n│   │   │   ├── AuthController.js    # Auth endpoints\n│   │   │   ├── WeatherController.js # Weather endpoints\n│   │   │   ├── UserController.js    # User endpoints\n│   │   │   └── CityController.js    # City endpoints\n│   │   ├── routes/\n│   │   │   ├── authRoutes.js        # /api/auth routes\n│   │   │   ├── weatherRoutes.js     # /api/weather routes\n│   │   │   ├── userRoutes.js        # /api/users routes\n│   │   │   ├── cityRoutes.js        # /api/cities routes\n│   │   │   └── index.js             # Route aggregation\n│   │   ├── utils/\n│   │   │   ├── validators.js        # Input validation\n│   │   │   ├── errorFormatter.js    # Error formatting\n│   │   │   ├── tokenGenerator.js    # JWT token generation\n│   │   │   └── weatherDataMapper.js # Data transformation\n│   │   ├── app.js                   # Express app setup\n│   │   └── server.js                # Server startup\n│   ├── tests/\n│   │   ├── unit/\n│   │   ├── integration/\n│   │   └── fixtures/\n│   ├── .env.example\n│   ├── package.json\n│   └── README.md\n│\n├── frontend/\n│   ├── src/\n│   │   ├── components/\n│   │   │   ├── Auth/\n│   │   │   │   ├── LoginForm.jsx\n│   │   │   │   ├── RegisterForm.jsx\n│   │   │   │   └── ProtectedRoute.jsx\n│   │   │   ├── Dashboard/\n│   │   │   │   ├── Dashboard.jsx\n│   │   │   │   ├── WeatherCard.jsx\n│   │   │   │   ├── CityGrid.jsx\n│   │   │   │   └── AddCityModal.jsx\n│   │   │   ├── Weather/\n│   │   │   │   ├── WeatherDetail.jsx\n│   │   │   │   ├── ForecastView.jsx\n│   │   │   │   └── CurrentWeatherDisplay.jsx\n│   │   │   ├── Search/\n│   │   │   │   ├── CitySearch.jsx\n│   │   │   │   └── SearchResults.jsx\n│   │   │   ├── Settings/\n│   │   │   │   ├── SettingsPage.jsx\n│   │   │   │   ├── PreferencesForm.jsx\n│   │   │   │   └── ThemeToggle.jsx\n│   │   │   ├── Common/\n│   │   │   │   ├── Header.jsx\n│   │   │   │   ├── Sidebar.jsx\n│   │   │   │   ├── LoadingSpinner.jsx\n│   │   │   │   ├── ErrorBoundary.jsx\n│   │   │   │   └── Notification.jsx\n│   │   │   └── Layout/\n│   │   │       └── MainLayout.jsx\n│   │   ├── pages/\n│   │   │   ├── LoginPage.jsx\n│   │   │   ├── RegisterPage.jsx\n│   │   │   ├── DashboardPage.jsx\n│   │   │   ├── WeatherDetailPage.jsx\n│   │   │   ├── SettingsPage.jsx\n│   │   │   └── NotFoundPage.jsx\n│   │   ├── store/\n│   │   │   ├── index.js\n│   │   │   ├── slices/\n│   │   │   │   ├── authSlice.js\n│   │   │   │   ├── weatherSlice.js\n│   │   │   │   ├── userSlice.js\n│   │   │   │   ├── citySlice.js\n│   │   │   │   ├── uiSlice.js\n│   │   │   │   └── settingsSlice.js\n│   │   │   ├── selectors/\n│   │   │   │   ├── authSelectors.js\n│   │   │   │   ├── weatherSelectors.js\n│   │   │   │   ├── citySelectors.js\n│   │   │   │   └── settingsSelectors.js\n│   │   │   └── thunks/\n│   │   │       ├── authThunks.js\n│   │   │       ├── weatherThunks.js\n│   │   │       ├── userThunks.js\n│   │   │       └── cityThunks.js\n│   │   ├── services/\n│   │   │   ├── api/\n│   │   │   │   ├── axiosInstance.js\n│   │   │   │   ├── apiClient.js\n│   │   │   │   ├── endpoints.js\n│   │   │   │   └── interceptors.js\n│   │   │   ├── auth/\n│   │   │   │   └── AuthService.js\n│   │   │   ├── weather/\n│   │   │   │   └── WeatherService.js\n│   │   │   ├── user/\n│   │   │   │   └── UserService.js\n│   │   │   └── city/\n│   │   │       └── CityService.js\n│   │   ├── hooks/\n│   │   │   ├── useAuth.js\n│   │   │   ├── useWeather.js\n│   │   │   ├── useCity.js\n│   │   │   ├── useSettings.js\n│   │   │   ├── useFetch.js\n│   │   │   └── useLocalStorage.js\n│   │   ├── styles/\n│   │   │   ├── index.css\n│   │   │   ├── variables.css\n│   │   │   ├── theme.css\n│   │   │   └── responsive.css\n│   │   ├── utils/\n│   │   │   ├── formatters.js\n│   │   │   ├── validators.js\n│   │   │   ├── constants.js\n│   │   │   └── helpers.js\n│   │   ├── config/\n│   │   │   ├── apiConfig.js\n│   │   │   └── appConfig.js\n│   │   ├── App.jsx\n│   │   └── index.jsx\n│   ├── .env.example\n│   ├── package.json\n│   ├── vite.config.js\n│   └── README.md\n│\n├── docker-compose.yml\n├── .gitignore\n└── README.md\n```\n\n---\n\n## **BACKEND COMPONENTS - DETAILED RESPONSIBILITIES**\n\n### **1. CONFIGURATION LAYER**\n\n#### **database.js** - Database Connection Management\n**Responsibility:** Initialize PostgreSQL/MongoDB connection pool, manage connections, handle reconnection logic\n```\n- Connection pooling with configurable pool size\n- Automatic reconnection on failure\n- Health check monitoring\n- Query execution wrapper\n- Connection lifecycle management\n```\n\n#### **cache.js** - Redis Cache Configuration\n**Responsibility:** Initialize and manage Redis cache for weather data and session storage\n```\n- Redis client initialization\n- TTL configuration for different data types (current: 1hr, forecast: 6hrs)\n- Cache key generation and management\n- Cache invalidation strategies\n- Connection pooling and error recovery\n```\n\n#### **environment.js** - Environment Variables\n**Responsibility:** Load, validate, and provide environment configuration\n```\n- Database credentials and connection strings\n- API keys for external weather services\n- JWT secrets and token expiry settings\n- Rate limiting configuration\n- CORS and security settings\n```\n\n---\n\n### **2. MIDDLEWARE LAYER**\n\n#### **authenticate.js** - JWT Authentication\n**Responsibility:** Verify JWT tokens and attach user context to requests\n```\n- Extract token from Authorization header\n- Validate JWT signature and expiry\n- Attach decoded user data to request\n- Handle token expiration and refresh\n- Support optional authentication routes\n```\n\n#### **errorHandler.js** - Global Error Handling\n**Responsibility:** Catch and format all application errors consistently\n```\n- Catch unhandled errors from routes and services\n- Format error responses with proper HTTP status codes\n- Log errors with context (user ID, endpoint, timestamp)\n- Distinguish between operational and programming errors\n- Sanitize sensitive information from error messages\n```\n\n#### **rateLimiter.js** - Request Rate Limiting\n**Responsibility:** Prevent abuse by limiting requests per IP/user\n```\n- General API limiter: 100 requests/15 minutes\n- Auth limiter: 5 login attempts/15 minutes\n- Weather API limiter: 50 requests/minute per user\n- Search limiter: 30 requests/minute per user\n- Redis-backed persistent rate limiting\n```\n\n#### **logging.js** - Request Logging\n**Responsibility:** Log all HTTP requests and responses for monitoring\n```\n- Log HTTP method, path, status code, and response time\n- Track user ID and IP address\n- Sanitize sensitive data (passwords, tokens)\n- Generate correlation IDs for request tracing\n- Structured logging for analytics\n```\n\n---\n\n### **3. DATABASE MODELS**\n\n#### **User.js** - User Account Management\n**Responsibility:** Define user schema and authentication methods\n```\nFields:\n- email (unique), password (hashed), username\n- firstName, lastName, profileImage, bio\n- preferences (temperature unit, theme, notifications)\n- emailVerified, passwordReset tokens\n- loginAttempts, accountLock, lastLogin\n- role (user/admin), isActive status\n\nMethods:\n- comparePassword() - Verify password during login\n- isAccountLocked() - Check if account is locked\n- incLoginAttempts() - Track failed login attempts\n- resetLoginAttempts() - Reset after successful login\n- createPasswordResetToken() - Generate password reset token\n- createEmailVerificationToken() - Generate email verification token\n```\n\n#### **City.js** - City Information\n**Responsibility:** Store city data with geographic coordinates\n```\nFields:\n- name, country, countryCode, state\n- latitude, longitude (for weather API calls)\n- timezone, population, isCapital\n- alternateNames, searchCount (popularity tracking)\n- timestamps for data freshness\n\nIndexes:\n- Compound unique index on (name, country, latitude, longitude)\n- Spatial index on coordinates for nearby city searches\n- Search count index for popular cities ranking\n```\n\n#### **UserCity.js** - User's City Preferences\n**Responsibility:** Link users to their tracked cities with custom settings\n```\nFields:\n- user (reference to User), city (reference to City)\n- isDefault (primary city), nickname (custom name)\n- alerts (temperature, precipitation, wind thresholds)\n- order (display sequence)\n\nMethods:\n- setAsDefault() - Make this the user's primary city\n- updateAlerts() - Modify alert thresholds\n- findUserCities() - Get all cities for a user\n- findDefaultCity() - Get user's primary city\n```\n\n#### **WeatherCache.js** - Cached Weather Data\n**Responsibility:** Store weather API responses to minimize external calls\n```\nFields:\n- city (reference), cacheType (current/forecast/hourly)\n- data (JSON weather information), source (API provider)\n- expiresAt (TTL index for auto-deletion)\n- hitCount (cache effectiveness metrics)\n\nMethods:\n- isExpired() - Check if cache data is stale\n- incrementHitCount() - Track cache usage\n- refresh() - Update with new data and reset TTL\n- findOrCreateCache() - Get or create cache entry\n- clearExpired() - Remove outdated entries\n```\n\n#### **APILog.js** - API Call Tracking\n**Responsibility:** Log all API requests for monitoring and debugging\n```\nFields:\n- endpoint, method, statusCode, responseTime\n- user (who made the call), requestSize, responseSize\n- errorMessage (if failed), ipAddress, userAgent\n- externalAPICall details (if calling third-party API)\n- TTL index for auto-deletion after 30 days\n\nPurpose:\n- Performance monitoring\n- Usage analytics\n- Error tracking and debugging\n- Rate limiting enforcement\n- Audit trail for security\n```\n\n---\n\n### **4. SERVICES LAYER**\n\n#### **AuthService.js** - Authentication Logic\n**Responsibility:** Handle user registration, login, and token management\n```\nMethods:\n- register(userData) - Create new user account\n  - Validate email uniqueness\n  - Hash password with bcrypt\n  - Generate JWT tokens (access + refresh)\n  - Return user profile and tokens\n\n- login(email, password) - Authenticate user\n  - Find user by email\n  - Verify password\n  - Update lastLogin timestamp\n  - Generate new tokens\n  - Return user and tokens\n\n- refreshToken(refreshToken) - Extend session\n  - Verify refresh token validity\n  - Generate new access token\n  - Return new token pair\n\n- changePassword(userId, oldPassword, newPassword) - Update password\n  - Verify old password\n  - Hash new password\n  - Save to database\n\n- resetPassword(email) - Initiate password reset\n  - Find user by email\n  - Generate reset token with 1-hour expiry\n  - Send reset email (integration point)\n  - Return reset token for frontend\n\n- logout(userId) - End session\n  - Optional: Add token to blacklist\n  - Clear client-side auth data\n```\n\n#### **WeatherService.js** - Weather Data Operations\n**Responsibility:** Fetch, cache, and serve weather data\n```\nMethods:\n- getWeatherByCityId(cityId, options) - Get current weather\n  - Check Redis cache first\n  - If cache miss, call external API\n  - Transform data to standard format\n  - Cache for 1 hour\n  - Return formatted weather data\n\n- getWeatherByCoordinates(lat, lon, options) - Weather by location\n  - Call external API with coordinates\n  - Transform response\n  - Return weather data\n\n- getWeatherForecast(cityId, days) - Get forecast\n  - Fetch forecast from external API\n  - Cache for 6 hours\n  - Return day-by-day forecast\n\n- getMultipleCitiesWeather(cityIds) - Batch fetch\n  - Parallel fetch for multiple cities\n  - Return array of weather data\n  - Optimize with concurrent requests\n\n- getWeatherAlerts(cityId) - Get active weather alerts\n  - Query external API for alerts\n  - Filter by location\n  - Return alert information\n\n- clearCache(city"}], "tool_failures": []}J&
